{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"head -100 docs/CURRENT_STATE.md; sed -n '265,510p' AGENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Current state\n\n**Clean Steps 1–3, current (2026-11-11).** Records: Step 1, [round log](../clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md) §§16–47; Step 2, [Step 2 log](../clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md) §§12–19.\n- **Step 1 configuration: c8, adopted by Alex (D387).** It runs DeepSeek Flash at high effort, with a 64,000-token output cap; a\n  format failure or a cut answer is resent once (D380). It carries Alex's decisions D382–D385:\n  - figures are conditions;\n  - material statements with no thesis are kept without links;\n  - only big matters open a thesis;\n  - no target prices.\n\n  [PRD §12](../clean-arch/PRD.md) holds its system prompt, closing check and schema; a run with no candidate files sends exactly the\n  accepted request.\n- **Acceptance (D386, [protocol](../clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/ACCEPTANCE-PROTOCOL.md)).** 50 fresh articles that no run,\n  old or new, had used: news from 2026-09-05 to 09-07, a holiday weekend with no NVIDIA posts. One draw; two readers and a third on\n  disputes.\n  - helpful 132/139 (core 83/83);\n  - wrongly opened theses 1 of 10;\n  - search 141/143 available repeat pairs, or 141/145 for the whole system (one 11-article story supplies 55 pairs, and revisions are\n    barely exercised);\n  - clear wrong merges 1/57, plus 2 overlaps;\n  - detail retention 22 = 22. This is a storage comparison: every record keeps its own text. It is not a usability test.\n\n  Dev ×3 on the frozen golden-v5 (a lead): helpful 214, 211 and 212 of 234; search 98.9–100%; clear wrong merges about 1%. Step 1\n  cost for the fresh set plus dev ×3: $4.20 at published rates.\n- **Steps 2 and 3** are built in isolation (`clean-arch/step2`, `clean-arch/step3`): search, comparison, grouping and later linking.\n  They are not integrated with production storage. **Step 4 (judging) has not passed** on the clean path: its ladder step is built and\n  measured (four Stage A runs, lines missed by 1 to 3 answers; D426), so nothing yet shows the clean system can judge an investment\n  view on its own questions.\n- **Step 2 is closed and frozen (Alex, D427, 2026-11-11;** [Step 2 log](../clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md) §§14–19**).** It goes\n  to production only with the whole clean path, after Step 4 meets its lines; `tests/test_frozen_clean_step2.py` guards its files. Its three lines were met at the acceptance above (one draw; \"later version\"\n  relations barely exercised), and no miss of the seeded end-to-end test (clean 18, 18, 17 against production 17, 15, 16) has\n  been traced to it (the two single-draw misses were diagnosed on 2026-11-11, below: neither traces to Step 2). What happened since the close-out of 2026-11-08:\n  - A change to Jev's wording for \"later version\" relations failed its line (42 calls, 2026-11-09) and tuning stopped.\n  - One wrong relation was traced to the judge: it put NVIDIA's answer to the Kyber report under the FY2027 revenue question;\n    sent both ways, the conclusion did not differ ([result](../clean-arch/step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10/RESULT.md)).\n  - Alex stopped work on that relation (D423) and asked for a fix to the rule that gives a \"later version\" the older record's\n    questions. Measured on the three saved draws ([round log](../clean-arch/step2-revision-links-2026-11-10/LOG.md)), removing the\n    rule was withdrawn: of the 24 links it wrote, two blind reader families call 19 context and 3 evidence, and one of the 3 is a\n    company's answer that would otherwise be missing beside four reports (with it rung 2, 2, 2; without it 2, 3, 2). **The rule\n    stays (D424).**\n  - **Open, recorded:** Jev's \"later version\" relation (9 of 30 join different statements in draw 1); the context links it carries\n    (19 of 24); wrong groups (at the line on one draw; the unprompted reading test never run); the \"Unverified quote\" mark not\n    shown to Jev (3 of 188); not decided, whether a company's answer must sit under every question its report is filed under.\n  - **Reopens when** Step 4 yields judged views on the clean path and a miss, or something a reader of a thesis sees, traces to\n    one of these. The round's measurement kit (replay of a saved draw, exact simulation of a writer rule, blind packets with\n    controls, a judgement sent both ways) is kept in the two folders above.\n- **The clean system's untraced end-to-end misses, diagnosed (2026-11-11;** [round log](../clean-arch/e2e-misses-2026-11-11/LOG.md)**).**\n  The China share question in draw 3 and the FY2028 revenue question in draw 2 (seeded test, D392). Both estimates sit on a rung\n  line. China: the same window-end request, re-sent, gives the miss twice and the right answer once (the judge's own variation at the\n  1% line); no H200 price is in any request. FY2028: draw 2's window-end request gives the miss 3 of 3 and draw 3's the right answer 3\n  of 3; draw 2's lacks records draw 3's holds (a \"41% in calendar 2027\" figure Step 1 filed under FY2027 only, \"$1 trillion of\n  Blackwell and Rubin visibility\", five infrastructure-demand records), not isolated which matters; FY2028 is the question whose filed\n  statements differ most between draws (47% shared, median 74%). Neither traces to Step 2. Refuted on the way: that a refused answer\n  re-asked caused the China miss. Observed defect of the frozen judge: it names the export-controls theme as a dependency of the China\n  question, 42 of 65 refusals in six draws, and the re-ask changed the rung 8 times (PRD 11, E4). No change proposed; 18 sends, $0.043.\n- **Open defects, by product impact** (reflection council, `council/av-codex.md`):\n  1. **The Ohio-guarantee yes/no question is never covered** in the three dev draws; a broader credit-support amount thesis opens\n     instead. Diagnosed (round log §48): the model folds the unsigned guarantee into the open aggregate thesis because the request\n     uses \"covers\" both for \"is evidence for\" and for \"already asks this question\". The same clause sits under link clutter.\n  2. **A revenue-share thesis was opened** (Vera Rubin's share of data-center revenue), the class-A boundary of D382.\n  3. **Link clutter.** A blind recheck of the 34 disputed fresh links found 19 weak and 2 wrong; 10 accepted links mixed in as controls were all useful; the other 49 links were not rechecked.\n     The model's own account names topic or theme overlap and inference chains, and c8's closing check never reads back a link. This is\n     a likely cause, with no fix proven. Alex approved designing a protected link check through the council; a first draft was stopped\n     because it would drop founding premises and contrary facts.\n  4. **Unverified passages:** 3 of 188 fresh records and 1–3 per dev draw. The mark now travels into Step 2's records, and a reader sees the found source text or an \"Unverified quote\" label. Jev's comparison input still carries the model's text without the mark; changing it changes measured Step 2 behaviour and needs its own measurement.\n  5. **The lidar policy thesis** recurs at the boundary (one dev draw in three).\n- **History.** These earlier states are superseded:\n  - the 2026-11-07 takeover (K5 → K6b; [takeover log](../clean-arch/takeover-2026-11-07/LOG.md));\n  - the 2026-11-08 close-out (K6b test 32/42; Step 2 first lines; [Step 2 log](../clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md) §12);\n  - the unfiled fix round and the c1–c7 arms (round log §§1–39).\n- **No run is live.** The branch is committed through the D388 line (round log §§48–59).\n\n**Clean Step 1 source investigation (2026-11-07):** A [source-loss census](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-LOSS-CENSUS.md) traces two separate losses in the historical cleaner and records reproducible corpus observations. Offline candidate comparisons expose both recovered content and source-identity or contamination risks. A subsequent [full-page diagnostic](../clean-arch/STEP1-FULL-PAGE-RESULTS.md) completed 102 calls on 17 selected articles and independent source-backed review. It exposes examples of both missing or misattributed source text and model errors that persist despite the right text being present. A Codex–Claude council is reviewing the results and earlier attempts; no source-cleaning candidate is adopted, and the source corpus and production defaults are unchanged.\n\nAlex has authorized correcting the test-source cleaner and test data when their defects are confirmed, while the frozen production configuration and ruler remain intact. The cleaner switched 615 originally fed articles off; a replay reproduces all 615, and direct inspection confirms an actual article excluded because its 9,874-character body was flattened to one line. Other examples include a wrong-site shell, paywall and long challenge code, so the false-exclusion count and a general article-identification repair remain to be established. The [council regroup](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-REGROUP-COUNCIL.md) and [source-preservation design](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PRESERVATION-DESIGN.md) describe an isolated candidate checked against all 34,084 records, with a fake-answer actual-runner handoff and provenance display in the replay renderer. The [five source-control calls](../clean-arch/STEP1-CAPTURE-CONTROLS-RESULTS.md) completed and were source-reviewed; two items contain summary details absent from their attached quotations, and one source-visible risk explanation was not returned. This is selected-case evidence, not a general quality result. Broader source-quality comparison, citation completeness and actual writer integration remain open.\n\n**Clean architecture Step 1 (2026-11-06, isolated work on `clean-arch`):** Alex reopened work with the clean architecture. An experimental prepared-source handoff now preserves the archived page, prior cleaned text, source-role decisions and selected-line mapping without changing the original database; quotations for prepared items must also occur contiguously in the original captured page. Two seven-item runs are available in the [clean architecture PRD](../clean-arch/PRD.md), one in the earlier selection order and one in recorded page-timestamp order. The source selector is not a production service and source ordering is not established event-arrival ordering. The runs expose unresolved semantic problems: citations can omit supporting facts despite an exact location match; model output can change a benchmark into a deployment, reverse a backup relation, omit a named customer or assign an unstated currency. A blinded 84-call check-placement/wording comparison and a 27-call same-article citation-completion diagnostic did not give a clean semantic fix and are not adopted. The latter missed an omitted connectivity condition and a reversed backup relationship, and left six expected evidence reviews unaddressed. A further five-round Codex–Claude council produced a narrowly scoped Step 1 link candidate, independently checked for prompt-contract drift. A six-article, 36-call blind comparison completed; the candidate still produced an explicitly self-contradictory link and both arms consistently omitted the same Kyber report and company response. It is not adopted and has not changed the active PRD prompt. A trace confirms that both the Kyber report and open Kyber thesis were supplied, and the raw model answers omitted the report and denial; the reason is not established. See ../poc/data/clean-step1-kyber-trace-2026-11-06/TRACE.md. An isolated six-call comparison showed that hiding the Kyber thesis did not recover the report or denial in any draw. A second six-call comparison returned them in 3/3 draws with the original Kyber paragraph alone and 0/3 with the full article; length, position and surrounding content changed together, so the reason is not isolated. Excerpt outputs have source-attribution limitations. Neither experiment changed state or established a production fix. (Superseded: the next task then was a whole-article coverage approach; the current next task is under \"One next task\".) See ../clean-arch/STEP1-IMPLEMENTATION-COUNCIL.md. The earlier four-round council agreed that no tested semantic fix is ready; its next investigation is a source-backed review of the 49-item historical run and its 160 evidence records, with overlapping issue flags and separate article-level omissions, then a separate comparison of the seven-item replays. See ../clean-arch/STEP1-COUNCIL-REVIEW.md. Preserve relevant evidence while identifying the next intervention; production/frozen history remains as described below. See [Step 1 run log](../clean-arch/STEP1-RUN-LOG.md) and [English reading page](../clean-arch/architecture.html).\n\n**Sealed (D379, 2026-11-06):** Alex asked to clean up and seal this version while he re-plans the system design. Work stops here and is sealed as it is: main's working tree is committed on branch `seal/2026-11-06` (tag `sealed-2026-11-06`) and merged into `main` on Alex's word (PR #10); the sealed split and two side experiments are pushed on their own branches (D379). No PRD 11 experiment is open, and the E1 next task below is withdrawn. The next task is Alex's re-planned system design.\n\n**E1 diagnosed (2026-11-06, Alex chose E1):** of 57 helpful matters frozen production wrote and then dropped, two readers agree on 17 link misses (4 core), 3 opening misses (1 core) and 24 small matters the standard itself drops; 10 are disputed on the fallback clause and 3 were quote refusals. Opening is not the experiment. The core of the link misses is the model reading a question's period, population or named configuration as a boundary; only 8 of the 13 window draws it dropped were lost to the product. No production change; $0.02 of probes. My recommendation was to fold that narrow change into the next extraction version; withdrawn by the seal (D379). Details: `docs/research/2026-11-06-e1-no-home-drops/README.md`, PRD 11 E1.\n\n**Split extraction sealed as a failed experiment (D378, 2026-11-06):** the split (a new-question call, an evidence call and record preparation) was benchmarked against the frozen poc-v108 and failed. Its stop line fired: helpful matters 156, 156, 159 against 166, 170, 162, with about 15% higher cost. One screened revision kept more noise than production. It is sealed in the worktree `hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review` (tag `split-extraction-failed-sealed-2026-11-06`), and nothing of it is in main. What it taught is written as proposed production experiments in `docs/prd/11-production-experiments-from-split.md`: E1 no-home helpful drops, E2 duplicate questions, E3 ladder checks with D186, E4 judge refusals, E5 D203's revision day, E6 the measurement kit. Each opens only on Alex's word.\n\n**Question-catalog limit removed (D377, 2026-11-05):** Alex also directed removal of the separate 150 KB catalog rejection. The research reader in this worktree now has neither the catalog nor evidence byte limit; it retains full scoped questions, historical boundaries, dependencies and evidence. A portable 326,996-byte catalog test returns all 400 new questions and expands evidence both after reading the catalog and directly; the old 150 KB guard fails the same test in a scratch copy. The saved 69-question pilot catalog and all 69 saved evidence expansions match their original content hashes. Details: `docs/research/2026-11-05-catalog-limit/`. The full suite remains pending until the paid seven-day run no longer competes for resources. The run remains in its isolated worktree and does not call this research reader.\n\n**Evidence reader limit removed (D376, 2026-11-05):** Alex directed removal of the reader's 1 MB evidence-expansion rejection. In this worktree, `research_context.Reader.expand` now returns the entire evidence payload without that cap, while the catalog's separate limit remained at that checkpoint; D377 subsequently removed it. On the saved pilot ledger, all 69 individual question expansions, the four-question 1,931,225-byte pilot request and the entire 3,454,076-byte catalog produce the exact same content as the pre-change high-limit baseline; the portable oversized-ledger test passes and fails when the old cap is restored in a scratch copy. Details and snapshot-specific measurements are in `docs/research/2026-11-05-reader-limit/`. The seven-day diagnostic runs in `/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/poc/data/split-fresh-seven-day-2026-11-05-v2/` with its pinned code; it does not call this research reader. Read its status through its `snapshot.sh`; do not edit its package code while it is live. This change is not an acceptance of seven-day extraction or judgement quality.\n\n**Start-state correction (2026-11-05):** Alex requires a research library established from real material available before the test start, then extraction against that state. The prior empty-library diagnostic cannot represent this case. Our own mistakes and the current 68-question provenance audit are in `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-parallel-refinement/own-mistakes-2026-11-05.zh.md`. Two new A-only calls were run on 2026-08-29 articles using the 68-question prior-day snapshot; both proposed the same aggregate supply-commitments topic. A source/context review judged it distinct from the existing specific SK Hynix question. A third A-only call on an author-body excerpt about DLSS 5, already tracked by v22, passed; the prompt also restricts software updates, so the reason is not established. No writer or dedup ran; source-history completeness remains unverified, and this is not scored acceptance. Details: ../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-parallel-refinement/start-state-diagnostic-2026-11-05.zh.md.\n\n**Measurement correction (2026-11-05):** Alex clarified that a gold-worthy topic already in the supplied library should not open again; an absent worthy topic should open. The earlier simple-A claim of a \"missed\" new topic was not scored against that rule and is withdrawn as a correctness conclusion. In the actual experiment, a Kyber topic was shown and passing follows Alex's topic-level rule; whether its exact release question captures the shipping milestone remains unverified. The experimental pre-article snapshots differ from the replay's day-start snapshots; 9 of 10 inspected examples differ. The current uncommitted replay default does not build a cold-start library; committed main HEAD still uses the old seed and startup filing path. Historical lexical coverage has a confirmed unrelated-topic match. The frozen gold and past scores remain unchanged. Audit: `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-parallel-refinement/measurement-context-scrub-2026-11-05.zh.md`.\n\n**Simple new-question diagnostic (2026-11-05):** At Alex's direction, an isolated prompt returned new questions plus article evidence without asking for product database fields. Four previously seen real dev articles each ran once: three returned one candidate, one returned none, all four quotes matched their source, and the gold-listed GPU backstop amount question was not proposed. Whether that omission is a new-topic miss depends on whether the existing library covers the topic. Two other candidates require source and independent-significance review; the actual experimental snapshot already had a Kyber topic, so its pass follows Alex's topic-level rule; whether its exact release question captures the shipping milestone remains unverified. This is not a production or full-pipeline acceptance. Details: `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-parallel-refinement/simple-new-question-results.zh.md`.\n\n**Split prompt structure v3 read diagnostic (2026-11-05):** One real reading-stage call on a previously seen article found the revenue/margin guidance and Trainium scale but omitted the gold China revenue/market-loss matter. The prewritten stop condition was triggered and the linking call was not sent. This is one draw and not a production or end-to-end result. See `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-parallel-refinement/structure-v3-read-result.zh.md`. D374 removes the model sampling field from active settings and default configs; historical config files and archives retain their original bytes.\n\n**Split prompt structure v2 small test (2026-11-05):** Thirty calls on two previously seen golden-v5 dev articles completed in `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review`. The blind model reader found complete helpful matters in the fresh control versus new A+B of 6/19 vs 10/19, 11/19 vs 7/19, and 9/19 vs 12/19. The new arm also retained more gold not-kept matters in each draw; B missed useful margin guidance and one answer reused IDs, with a demonstrated matching collision. This is not a production acceptance. See `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-parallel-refinement/structure-v2-results.zh.md` and `reports/2026-11-05-parallel-structure-v2.html`.\n\n**Split extraction small test (2026-11-05):** At Alex's request, the isolated `hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review` worktree ran two real golden-v5 articles once through each split lane. An independent model reader found 7 of 19 helpful gold matters fully retained, two partial, two written then dropped, eight missed, and one retained gold not-kept matter. Three saved v108 draws on these articles retained 7, 9 and 12 of 19, but used 22 seeded questions while the new test used 8/10-question snapshots; these are not directly comparable. The experiment remains unaccepted; see `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-parallel-refinement/small-scored-test-20261105.md` and `reports/2026-11-05-split-small-test.html`.\n\n- **The extraction standard** (piece 1) is the extraction step's PRD, signed by Alex on 2026-10-29 (D243: \"其他几条的意见我都ok，sign off\"),\n  which replaced the first version (D229: \"按照这套标准来开始做测量，这条标准不要漂移\"). It holds the ledger's three records, the five question\n  types, the opening tests, the evidence rule and its reject list, source tiers, weight, and how a prompt change is written, measured and\n  iterated. No arm, gold, judge or prompt adds a rule, an example or a weight the page does not hold; a change is a recorded decision in\n  Alex's words first, then a new version of the page, then a drift review.\n- **A ruler or gold that is built and reviewed is never changed again** (D261). Reviewed means readers who did not write it have read it\n  against the decisions and Alex has signed it. A ruler under construction is edited only until that review, and nothing is scored\n  against it before.\n- **The ruler is Alex's, never your own.** Gold, unit and the judge's reading are checked against what the product uses and fixed with\n  Alex before the first arm. A standard or reference you write gives every sentence its source (the signed standard, a decision, a PRD)\n  or lists it for Alex's decision with a lean; settling wording is no licence to change behaviour. After each rewrite, a read-only Codex\n  review against the decisions looks for unsourced rules, contradictions and misquotes, round after round until only wording-level\n  findings remain; clarity is tested apart, by independent readers on cases fixed before the text changes. A failed registered acceptance\n  stops the line and goes to Alex with its census; the next arm is never designed alone.\n- **Nobody grades their own change with a ruler still being corrected.** The reference is one Alex can read, reviewed and frozen before\n  the arms; a number scored against a ruler its author keeps correcting is not a conclusion. Meaning is judged by a reader who did not\n  write the change; code checks only structure and counts (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"我根本无法相信你的评价\").\n- **A new gold** (only for a new ruler version Alex opens). The unit is fixed before the first send (for extraction, one research matter\n  in one article, which several records may express; signed standard §11) and the gold is written from the complete material the model\n  sees before any answer is read. Each item holds the exact source span (checked by code), the standard line it follows, its weight under the signed rule and, where\n  proposals are pending, its weight under them with the proposals it depends on named.\n  A blind second reader reads the same sources; every disagreement is decided against the source and its reason recorded. The gold is\n  frozen with its sha256 and never edited after a send. Model-authored gold and model judges are labelled as such. A held-out set no arm\n  has seen is in from the first arm.\n- **Measure the stick before using it:** control against a second control, the criterion's null estimated (a conjunction over many items\n  fails by chance), and its workload sized from its rules. Tune on dev; score test once per configuration.\n\n### 7.2 Reading results\n\n- **A score is a lead; the traces are the measurement.** Every measurement has a score, and every time you read the traces yourself: the\n  raw answer beside the article for every missed helpful entry, and a sample of the extras and of the hits; historical gold keeps its original labels. The scorer\n  hard-codes no rule of the standard: it reads the gold file it is given, prints the gold's and the standard's sha256, and refuses a gold\n  made for another version; scores are compared only on the same gold. Do not write a new scorer to judge a probe: read the traces yourself (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n  \"不要写评分器这个之前就出问题过，你自己读trace 来分析\"). Alex, 2026-10-29 (D244): \"我觉得这是最容易出错的问题；你非常容易写死，我们在改的过程中如果drift你会一直用久的标准来衡量，这边需要有打分，但是“一定”要你自己下去看trace这是必须，记起来\".\n- **The ruler counts only what it was built to count.** Before a quality claim, a reader who did not write the change also reads the\n  fields the product stores (original day, original speaker, tier, the summary's hedges) and what the next step does with the record\n  (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"现在到底质量怎么样你深度的解析不要只是看尺子\").\n- Read the judges' reasons, not only the scores, and pick the next fix from the largest cause. Open the samples behind a metric's largest\n  values before reading it, and write down what a derived number reduces to.\n- **Report every number, regressions first.** For future evidence evaluation, combine the existing gold's core and supporting entries as helpful, use its not-kept entries as unhelpful, and leave optional entries neutral (D372). Count one research matter in one article (D250), not raw sentences. Retain the old labels and scores in historical results, and do not silently relabel the frozen gold. One quantity per table column. A comparison of\n  totals uses three draws; a count from one draw is labelled one draw and shows a mechanism, not a difference between arms. Lead with the\n  mechanism and the share of its class it explains, then the fix.\n- **Read what was dropped.** A statement the pipeline drops is thrown away with its reason, never parked on a side list; evaluation\n  reads the dropped statements by hand, classifies them by the mechanism that would have kept them, and fixes the largest class upstream\n  (D209: \"if it doesn't matter, just fucking throw it away … if there are false positives that got thrown away … you got to pick it up\").\n- **Measure end to end before a step's arm, and read the parked designs first.** A step's noise that the next step removes is not the\n  defect, and a step's recall that the next step throws away is. Before any arm on one step: the production replay through the whole path\n  on the gold window, the count at the step the product reads, and the decisions on the topic read for a parked fix (Alex, 2026-10-31:\n  \"make sure we are not going around in circles using wrong ruler and wrong prompts that don't work\"). Before a phase targets one step,\n  the upside of that step done perfectly is measured where the product is judged: the judge is given the gold's own evidence, built by\n  the production code, a few sends (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"我很不开心你的失败，为什么，深度多轮检讨记录，想思路突破\").\n- **Read what was kept against the gold, blind, before the next noise arm.** The not-kept gold entries a version keeps are judged by a\n  reader who wrote neither the gold nor the prompt, mixed with controls it cannot tell apart; where it parts from the gold, the standard\n  is unclear or the gold misreads it, and that goes to Alex before any arm counts it as noise (Alex, 2026-10-31: \"你再次重新检查尺子，看看是不是这些留下的还有歧义；然后再思考怎么降低noise\").\n- Pair every structural check with its semantic one. Run a data rule over its whole input range and on cases it was not tuned on. Weigh\n  a case by what it carries in the product, not by count.\n- A claim about a population (\"the data is clean\") rests on a code sweep of the whole population and an independent read of a fresh\n  random sample, never on the pages the author looked at.\n- Cost is priced from tokens at the published rates (`hivemind.model.PRICES`, cached input at `model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE`), never from a\n  stored `cost_usd`; say which rates a projection uses.\n\n### 7.3 Iterating\n\n- **One class at a time** (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"你一类一类改，快速迭代然后测regression\"). Count the misses by mechanism; take the largest\n  class; trace it to the sentence that causes it; change one thing aimed at that class; run the whole bench (a prompt change alters every\n  request) against the previous version; read every regression to its raw answer. The pages that showed the failure locate its\n  mechanism; only the whole bench (every set, every draw) accepts the change.\n- **Name the effect on the judgement first.** Every proposed change states the effect it is expected to have on a reader or on the final\n  judgement, and is tested there where possible; a step's own counts do not decide it alone. A fix that keeps moving its error to\n  neighbouring cases stops being tuned on that set (Alex, 2026-11-09: \"感觉现在一直在修一些mknor的原地打转，你是不是要思考下现在具体还差什么high priority big impact 的需要做？\";\n  he approved this rule the same day, D391).\n- **A model call is a sampler.** Re-send a stored request before calling its answer a defect. Totals and acceptance come from at least\n  three samples beside a fresh control; a bar the control fails against itself judges nothing. A direct-read pass\n  (one send per article, every answer read beside its source; D238) locates mechanisms; its counts are one draw and are labelled so.\n- **A written log.** One row per arm: hypothesis, change, numbers against the control (regressions first), kept or not. Refuted arms and\n  your own mistakes stay in it; the next session starts from its last row.\n- **Own the loop, within what Alex agreed.** When the direction is agreed and no stop is in force (`CURRENT_STATE.md`), push your own\n  hypotheses through $0 checks and probes of a few cents on stored cases without asking. A registered test, an end-to-end run, or\n  anything that departs from the agreed plan starts on his word; a result that contradicts the hypothesis stops the line and goes to him\n  (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\"). While he is not active (D439), \"his word\" is the council's\n  recorded consensus, and a stopped line goes to the council for re-assessment.\n- **Council before every change is sent.** A prompt, schema, code or criterion change, including one found by reading a probe, is a new\n  arm. It goes to an independent Codex read and a challenge round before its first send, and its result goes to a challenge round\n  before the next change. Reading the traces and the model's own account locates a fix; it does not review it (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n  \"你这些改动有我你有好好的跑council 再下手\").\n  Every round's reasoning and decisions are reflected on in the council until there is a consensus; the decision is recorded, and\n  the next test goes straight ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals, with every trace read by you yourself and not only\n  by readers (Alex, 2026-11-10: \"你应该跑council loop 来reflect 你每一轮的思路还有决策，需要你打成共识，记录决策，向前直行测试。不要drift,我们有PRD和量化目标，\n  你自己作为llm 下去看所有trace\").\n- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\n  work at a high level before any full analysis or stability test is built (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"don't overspend resources on wasting time.\n  We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we dive into do the full\n  analysis stability test. This is a principle you should remember\"). A day or week slice before any whole-corpus run; preflight on\n  stored data before any paid run (§5); no edit while a run is live (§9). A paid run measures a configuration; it never tries a fix.\n  Before each send, write what it can still change in the decision and which risk the cheaper check left uncovered; a replicate or\n  control that only re-measures noise or a settled comparison is not sent, and a fix is not sent before the model's own account and the\n  request locate where the decision is made (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"你跑这么多次真的有意义吗\"; \"我感觉你在为了跑而跑\"). Several fixes on one\n  base are each proved on stored data in minutes and then run together once (Alex, 2026-11-02: \"快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\"; D266).\n- **One recommendation, one test.** What reaches Alex as the next step of work is one recommendation and one test of it, reached after\n  rounds of review (Claude's own, Codex's, an independent reader's) on the traces until a round finds nothing serious; never a menu of\n  arms or options, never a conclusion the next probe overturns (a choice that changes what the system does still goes to him with its\n  options and a recommendation, Authority and scope) (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"就测试一种，一次 … 你就没有自己看5轮review，能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议？\").\n  An agreed recommendation is first challenged by an independent reader on the concrete evidence behind it (\"why you give\n  recommendations for this. What did you see exactly?\"). A review round reads a rule as its author meant it; only a send shows how the\n  model applies it: before a registered test, the changed request is sent on the cases that motivated it, a few cents.\n- **A failed arm is diagnosed before the next one.** When an arm fixes its class and regresses another, write the root cause first: the\n  process error (what grew, what the small sample did not guard) and the mechanism, traced to the raw answers and the model's account,\n  never a guess stated as the cause. A small sample guards every class the change can move, not only its own. When a fix keeps moving\n  another class, the call is doing several jobs: move the rule to its owner (a field's definition sits in the schema beside the field)\n  rather than add a sentence (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"那你这些修改都是失败的呀，为什么，根因，你要检讨然后再接着尝试。我觉得你已经陷入deep loop 了\").\n  A failed step of a plan is fixed and re-run at that same step: its failures are the work list, and nothing later in the plan and no\n  substitute plan starts before it passes (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"你为什么要drift? 你现在明明还有这么多的问题要fix,你到底知不知道你要fix什么？\").\n  Before a fix is proposed, write which goal the mechanism still serves and what the product already gives for it; a measurement that\n  removes the reason a mechanism exists retires the mechanism instead of starting its repair (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"I told you to think about\n  it and you're giving me suggestions that you reject yourself\").\n- **Before a version is rejected, the rejection is checked.** Every failed or refused answer behind a \"did not pass\" is read against its\n  source and put down as the model's error or the measuring rule's or check's error; a rule or check that refuses right answers is fixed,\n  and a version that already meets the goal (what it was built to fix is fixed, nothing that was right turned wrong) is not dropped for a\n  stricter rule a later review added. Alex, 2026-11-05: \"你到底是不是再搬石头砸自己的脚？各种reject自己，你确定是正确的rejection 吗？你又下去看trace吗？\";\n  \"你不能每次都这样判错然后浪费我时间，我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信下一步你要跑什么才能收敛\".\n- **Correct, then cheap.** Make the pipeline right and stable before any cost, speed or throughput work; report cost as a baseline only\n  (Alex, 2026-10-25).\n\n## 8. Product thinking\n\n- Think like a hedge-fund analyst. A thesis is an argued view about the business and the world; its stance comes from the argument\n  weighed against what is priced. Extract the few metrics or segments that carry it; financial-statement lines are its evidence, never its\n  definition.\n- **Lean cautious, catch the increment.** Most of what an item says is noise: not everything is evidence and not everything is a lead. A\n  typical claim or background line is common knowledge (what an analyst following the company knew before the item) and is not kept\n  without a number and a specific narrative; new information that changes an answer is never missed. Alex, 2026-10-29 (D243):\n  \"不是什么事情都是惊弓之鸟需要抽取，杂音还是很大的，我们整体应该倾向谨慎不要看什么都是线索的感觉，但是同时我们要敏感一些新的信息带来的增量不要错过\".\n- **A senior analyst's granularity.** A question is a bet an analyst would hold a card for: a big matter, never trivia (a deal, product or\n  project opens one only when its scale can change revenue, profit, cash or credit risk). Small matters open no question, and whether\n  their statements are kept follows the evidence rule; wordings, deadlines, milestones and periods of one bet are one question, and a\n  statement carried by several outlets is one statement (how code applies it: §3, Identity). Two questions stay apart only when their answers can move apart and an analyst\n  would bet on each separately (D248). Alex, 2026-10-30: \"我觉得核心就是这个颗粒度的把控要符合一个高端的hedge fund analyst 的思维。不要搜集一堆鸡毛蒜皮的事情，要看重要的大事，合并整合关键的信息，这个是这个步骤的原则\".\n- The extraction standard (§7.1, piece 1) is the step's standard. Its two sources are applied before designing a prompt, evaluation or\n  change (D228): the thesis library's four evidence tiers (`docs/prd/06-views.md`, Four evidence tiers) and the investment-question\n  reasoning in the 90-thesis review (`research_notes/对冲基金论点粒度与金标/codex-challenger.md`, section 1; research, not a replacement for\n  recorded decisions). Source type and what a claim can support are separate judgments; no tier has a fixed score. Ask what revenue,\n  profitability, cash risk or competitive position the information can change; then separately decide whether it supports an existing\n  question or merits a new one. Indirect, incomplete and forecast information is evidence under the routing rules; none of those\n  properties, nor an inability to open a new question, alone makes it worthless.\n- Evaluate the overall research judgment against the source, the existing question and the evidence. Gold examples teach the reasoning\n  and its boundaries; reasonable alternative wording, evidence strength and inference are allowed (D226, D228). Record material factual\n  errors, unsupported assumptions and downstream losses separately. Do not turn a review's questions, output labels or optional details\n  into an automatic all-or-nothing score. Missing market expectations or historical context means that aspect was not tested, not that\n  it passed or failed.\n- When a thesis-quality check fails, look first at the unit of thought (are these the arguments that move the stock?), not deeper into\n  the numbers. Numbers are verified by code where they exist.\n- Outcomes are tracked and shown, never a gate on what a view may say. Missing data is \"no data to verify\", never a pass or a fail. A\n  repeat is not new evidence, and model agreement is not corroboration.\n\n## 9. Workspace and operations\n\n- Inspect a path before writing to it; new stored data gets a new, dated name; chain guarded steps with `&&`. Deleting stored data needs\n  Alex's request, a backup, exactly identified items and a log entry.\n- Absolute paths. Commands run under zsh: pass a list as an array. No foreground `sleep`.\n- Preserve existing and concurrent changes: never reset, clean or stash work that is not yours. Never run parallel agents that edit\n  shared modules.\n- When Alex names a step, the test is that step alone through its own harness (extraction: stored requests re-sent, answers sifted,\n  scored against the gold). A full-pipeline run, a registered test, or a paid send beyond the probes of a few cents an agreed direction\n  allows (§7.3) starts only on his explicit word (Alex, 2026-10-27: \"我不是要你看下step 1抽取到底行不行？\").\n- A long paid run is launched detached in a new session with a log and pid file, after checking machine and network health; nothing heavy\n  runs beside paid calls. A gate runs on a snapshot no one is editing.\n- Never open a live run's databases: run `sh <run folder>/snapshot.sh` and query the snapshot.\n- No edit to package code or prompt files while any run is live: the parallel day's manifest hashes every `.py` and prompt file and\n  fails the day. Edit in another worktree or wait.\n- Experiment harnesses send concurrently (a thread pool of 8; the archive is thread-safe); serial sends waste the wall clock Alex is\n  waiting on.\n- **Run settings** (`scripts/replay.py`): extraction requests prepared 16 at a time (`--workers`; the measurement launcher passes its\n  `HIVEMIND_WORKERS` there), Jev matching 8 at a time (`--jev-workers`), judgements 32 at a time (`judging.JUDGE_WORKERS`); a model call\n  times out after 180 s and is tried up to three times.\n  The three draws of a measurement run at once, one launcher each (`docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/harness/run_arm.sh`). Measured\n  timings: `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`, \"Run settings and timing\".\n- Report results as they land; scope delegated work so a first useful result returns within 20–30 minutes.\n- Services for testing run on the host (README, \"Run the service for testing\"): on this Mac the VPN gives Docker containers no outbound\n  internet, so a model or embedding call fails inside Docker. Start them with a log and pid file, check them with\n  `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8788/days`, and stop what you started before handing over. Changing Docker or VPN networking is Alex's call.\n- Credentials never appear in Git, documents, logs, prompts, stored data, URLs or command arguments; they are kept in the owner-only file\n  `~/.config/hivemind/credentials.json`, outside the repository. Never raise a spending cap, and never switch a provider or model\n  silently.\n\n## 10. Rebuilding from ../tn-hivemind\n\n- Bring the system over one piece at a time; the product runs end to end at every step.\n- The old code is a source of requirements and stored cases, not a template. Before porting a piece, write what it does, who reads what\n  it writes, and which parts were patches (by their census); port the mechanism, leave the patches. A piece arrives with only the tests\n  that trace to its requirements, and an old rule arrives with the code it governs, as a check where code can hold it.\n\n## 11. Design documents and decisions\n\nThe design is the page `docs/system-design.html` (data in `docs/system-design/new-*.js`), one PRD per module in `docs/prd/` (index\n`README.md`; the extraction standard page sits beside PRD 05) and the decisions. The documents say what the code must do; code that\ndeparts from them waits for a decision.\n\n- The page data is the one source: a PRD block marked `generated` comes from it and is never edited by hand.\n- **Decisions.** `docs/DECISIONS.md` states what is decided now, by module, and gives every decision number's status;\n  `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` holds each decision's full record (Alex's words, what was decided, what was done) and is only appended to. A\n  new decision takes the next number: its record is appended to the log and its entry added to or changed in `docs/DECISIONS.md` in the\n  same change, the entry it replaces marked superseded in the index; the PRD that owns the rule is changed in the same change.\n- After any change, refresh by reasoning: re-read every module in the order and with the four questions of `docs/prd/README.md` (D22), so\n  that page, PRDs and decisions say the same thing, and list each inconsistency fixed. `python3 docs/check.py` runs last and checks only\n  mechanically; its pass is never the refresh.\n- Design every data path from what a view (thesis) needs, never from what the data offers: no number warehouse (D24, D28).\n- Write for a reader who did not follow the discussion: one concrete example, processes as step cards and decisions as trees; every\n  detail page links to its PRD. Maintained documentation, new product text and the pages written for Alex's review are in English (D163;\n  Alex, 2026-11-05: \"不，用英文吧\", D368); source quotations keep their language.\n- A rule is written in full in one place, its owner; summaries, other modules and the glossary name it or point to it without restating\n  its conditions, so a change lands once. A finding that one sentence missed a change is a class: count every place that states the same\n  thing before the first edit (§1).\n- Codex reviews read-only: `codex exec -s read-only -C <repo> --skip-git-repo-check --ephemeral -o <out> - < <prompt>`. The prompt names\n  the scope, the governing documents and what is out of scope; its report is a lead (§1).\n- Before a freeze, review in rounds. Each round runs read-only reviews by angle: an end-to-end simulation of realistic items,\n  state-by-event tables, wording against the glossary, whether an engineer could build each step from the text, every rule against the\n  decisions, an attack on Claude's own findings, a new reader answering questions, every change read in context, and line-by-line reads\n  by module. Each finding is checked against the text before a change; rounds go on until one finds nothing; then the freeze is recorded\n  and the design sealed.\n\n## Before finishing a slice\n\n0. No file of the frozen ruler (§7.1) has changed: `python3 -m pytest tests/test_frozen_rulers.py` is green.\n1. The touched suites, the structural checks and then the full suite pass; for a documents-only change, the reasoning refresh and then\n   `python3 docs/check.py`. A red suite is fixed before a handoff, whoever's code it is.\n2. `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md` holds the status, the open defects and the one next task; a status update retires the paragraphs it replaces.\n   A changed choice is recorded as a decision (§11).\n3. A lesson Alex states is written at the decision it governs in this file, in his words, in the same slice.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; sed -n '11210,11285p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && cat PAID-GATE-RESULT.md codex-r49.md codex-r51.md && nl -ba REPAIR-DESIGN.md | sed -n '140,245p'\"","aggregated_output":"# judging-v13 paid gate: result (D733)\n\n**STOP.** Every one of the 72 answers was refused by the code checks: 36 scored first attempts and 36 diagnostic retries. Nothing\nwas published, and the joint arm is usable in 0 of 9 pairs against the registered 8 of 9.\n\nThe result does not answer the question the gate was built for: does judging related number questions in one call give better\nnumbers than judging each alone? It shows that the answer format, as the request stated it, could not be filled. Most refusals are\nrules the request never stated, or checks that refuse right answers. A few are the model's own errors.\n\n- **Run:** `poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/`, sent once (D732) with gpt-6-luna. The ledger records 72 attempts and\n  $0.3677 of the $0.50 ceiling: $0.1554 for the first attempts and $0.2124 for the retries. Every attempt finished with status\n  `answered`, so the result is complete, not INCOMPLETE.\n- **The blind reading** was not run. The registered brief says \"A card that has no answer cannot be usable\", and every card has\n  none, so the readers cannot change the verdict.\n- **Council round 48:**\n  - `round48-brief.md`;\n  - `claude-r48.md`, Claude's reflection, written first;\n  - `codex-r48.md`, an independent fresh read-only Codex session that reproduced every refusal from the journals and the requests.\n\n## 1. Census (first attempt → retry; Codex's count, which corrects Claude's)\n\n| Attempt | Arm | Answers | Structure (C7) messages / answers | Stopped at the structure check |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| First | Joint | 9 | 39 / 9 | 9 |\n| First | Separate | 18 | 47 / 18 | 17 |\n| First | Single | 9 | 13 / 9 | 8 |\n| Retry | Joint | 9 | 40 / 9 | 9 |\n| Retry | Separate | 18 | 41 / 18 | 14 |\n| Retry | Single | 9 | 12 / 9 | 6 |\n\n`check()` returns early after any structure error, so most source, arithmetic and compatibility checks never ran on these answers.\n\n**Prose where the check expects an id**, counted by occurrence:\n\n| Field | First | Retry |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| `answers[].outcome` | 45 of 45 | 45 of 45 |\n| `answers[].reference.figure` | 39 | 32 |\n| `figures[].evidence` (139 of them on source figures, where C1 needs a passage id) | 175 | 133 (95) |\n| `figures[].bridge` | 49 | 44 |\n| `converts`, `disputed`, `inputs` | 3 | 3 |\n\n**Not one of the 90 member answers named a figure as its outcome**, in either journal. This failure alone refuses every answer.\nThe retries did not repair it. They carried the first attempt's reasons, and the early return had hidden this reason on most\nanswers.\n\n## 2. Mechanism\n\n1. **The format's rules live in `calc_check.py`, not in the request.**\n   - The sent schema carries 7 descriptions: `what`, `basis`, `kind`, `expression`, `relation`, `bridge` and `reference`.\n   - These fields have none: `value`, `low`, `high`, `bound`, `unit`, `evidence`, `component`, `inputs`, `operation`, `signs`,\n     `disputed`, `basis_text`, `rests_on`, `converts`, `scenario`, `outcome` and `rung`.\n   - The check enforces closed conventions on them:\n     - ids, not prose, in `evidence`, `outcome`, `reference.figure`, `bridge` and `disputed`;\n     - the unit spellings `USD bn`, `%` and `x`;\n     - a value or a range, never both (all 52 such refusals gave both);\n     - the period label `H1`;\n     - `share`, not `product`, for a percentage;\n     - each operation's operand count;\n     - `signs` only on `sum` and `roll_forward`.\n   - The descriptions of `bridge` (\"an estimate stating the conversion …\") and `reference` (\"An external figure, or a calculation …\")\n     read as asking for prose. The check reads both as ids.\n   - REQUEST-AUDIT.md says \"field definitions moved to the schema\". Most did not reach the sent bytes.\n2. **Some checks refuse right answers.** Each case was exposed by replaying a stored answer with the earlier refusal removed on a\n   copy:\n   - Q1 + Q2 Data Center revenue = \"FY2027 first half\" is refused, because the period parser reads only `H1`.\n   - FY2026 Q4 × (1 + the source's stated 65% year-over-year growth) is refused for want of a bridge. The check excuses\n     `apply_growth` only under a family `same_base` relation.\n   - $411 billion × 92.5% is computed by `product` as 38,017.5.\n   - \"well over $300 billion\" is refused because the parser starts one word later.\n   - $1.05 trillion is compared with bands in billions.\n3. **Model errors seen in the sample:**\n   - a 15% growth rate supported by forecasts computed from that same rate, a cycle;\n   - $25 billion and $18 billion of commitments added, although the source does not establish that the $18 billion comes on top of\n     the $25 billion;\n   - a full-year residual taken as a forecast. This is a judgement for a reader, not for code.\n4. **Diagnostic on copies (Claude's script, labelled a probe, not a count of right answers).**\n   - The script mechanically corrected the format classes.\n   - Result: 25 of 36 first attempts passed the early structure check, 9 had no structure error at all, and 0 would publish. The\n     retries gave the same counts.\n   - It guesses links from matching amounts, so it does not show how many answers a repaired request would get right.\n\n## 3. Process error\n\nAGENTS §6 says: \"Check before the send, at no cost. Write one answer that follows the prompt and run every code check on it.\"\n\n- **What the $0 gate proved.** Its passing answer, like the rehearsal's clean fixture, was written by someone who knew the check's\n  ids, units and period spellings. It proved that the harness accepts a conforming answer, not that the request teaches one.\n- **The missed step.** A writer who sees only the outgoing request writes the answer, and that first output goes through the real\n  checks. Each refusal must then point to the sentence of the request that states its rule.\n- **What the eight council rounds covered.** Rounds 47 to 47h reviewed the harness. None read the request as the model reads it\n  against the check.\n- **A wrong field in the mid-run diagnosis.** Claude told Alex the prose sat in `rests_on`. It sat in `evidence`, `bridge`, `outcome`\n  and `reference`.\n\n## 4. Council consensus: one recommendation, one test (for Alex's choice)\n\n**Recommendation.** Keep the STOP. Alex opens one bounded repair of judging-v13's request and checks:\n- each field's rule goes in the schema beside the field;\n- ids, units and choices become enums where the strict schema can hold them (the request already uses an id enum for `cites`);\n- the demonstrated period, arithmetic, parser and unit failures are fixed;\n- the checks for real scope changes, unstated assumptions and cycles are kept.\n\nClaude first leaned toward having code send the model a catalogue of the passages' numeric expressions. The council set that aside.\nThe parser's known omissions would become missing evidence, and the catalogue leaves the outcome-link failure untouched.\n\n**Test ($0, before any send).** One blind conformance test, registered before it runs:\n1. **Correct examples and broken counterparts are fixed first.** The examples cover a joint pair, its two separate answers, and the\n   three singleton shapes. The broken counterparts include a wrong number, a wrong period or scope, an unresolved overlap and a\n   circular calculation.\n2. **An independent writer sees only the new request** and writes the answers. The writer's first outputs go through the real\n   harness without hand edits.\n3. **Stop conditions.** The test stops if any correct form is refused, if any planted defect gets through its check, or if the\n   writer needs a rule the request does not state.\n4. **The 72 stored answers check individual fixes** where the intended figure and source can be identified. A guessed link earns no\n   credit.\n\nA clean result earns a request to Alex to send the same 36-request comparison again under a new decision, with D725's lines\nunchanged. The alternative is to close judging-v13. poc-v118 is already the product (D690), and the number answers stay a known\ndefect.\n**Round 49 finds serious issues. Revise the design before writing code.** I replayed the proposed growth rule in memory. It accepted a source’s **12% sequential growth** as **12% year-over-year growth** once the answer relabelled the rate. The repair would let the answer supply its own proof that the rate applies.\n\nI rebuilt the original plan byte for byte, checked the stored first answers and retries, and reran the existing gate at $0. All 87 baseline cases passed. The counterexamples below test the proposed rules in memory.\n\n## Blockers\n\n1. **§3.2 trusts the answer’s growth label.** I used the actual 12% sequential guidance in `e3943`, labelled it `FY2027 Q4 vs FY2026 Q4`, and applied it to a $100B prior-year base. The current check refused it. A literal implementation of §3.2 accepted $112B. The positive control has a related problem. `e5162`’s exact quote is “and 65% growth in Q4.” Its summary supplies *year over year*. Under the quote-only rule, that item alone cannot prove the comparison. The design needs to say where both periods come from for a source rate, how a computed rate gets its periods from its operands, and when an assumption is required. A2 needs the **falsely relabelled** rate as well as the honestly labelled rate applied to the wrong base. Replacing the existing `same_base` exception also broke G4 in my replay. Keeping that exception as written leaves a shortcut triggered by any `same_base` relation in the family. [Growth check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:438) · [12% source](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan.json:8722) · [65% as shown](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan.json:2387) · [G4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/gate.py:261)\n\n2. **§3.4 verifies where the words occur and can still reverse their meaning.** In my replay, `not be over $300 billion` passed as `> $300B`. The contained match was `over $300 billion`. `-12% sequentially` also passed as positive `12%`. A qualifier can sit outside both spans. In `$300 billion or more`, the parser extracts an exact `$300 billion`, so both versions accept a point. “Exactly one extracted expression” can also admit a second quantity the parser misses, such as `$300 billion and 50 units`. Keep the positive controls for `well over` and the longer Q4 phrase. Register the sign, negation, trailing qualifier and second-quantity cases before settling what the check can certify. [Repair §3.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:61) · [Extractor and C1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:12)\n\n3. **The blind test currently supplies the wrong question for E, and S needs its year corrected.** `old-2/8287` exists and really is `v41`, but it asks whether the Fed will raise rates. `old-3/8287` asks about an investment. Vera CPU FY2028 is `v41` in `old-3`, where I found 20 alternatives to paid call 9166. S’s `old-3/9043` correctly asks about four hyperscalers, for **calendar 2026**. Reusing the paid S key would ask for **CY2027** in `Outcome keys`. The render path accepts a caller-supplied member ID and copies the archived heading without checking that they describe the same question. Register the archive, call ID, question, period and ladder together. [Blind inputs](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:104) · [Paid case declarations](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:39) · [Render path](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:85)\n\n## Rules still missing from the request\n\nI walked every refusal in `calc_check.py`. The proposal covers unique figure IDs, the individual field enums, figure ID versus passage ID for the renamed fields, and the exact outcome key in substance. The existing request already prints all four parts of the outcome key. The following rules are missing, incomplete or stated differently from what code enforces. [Proposed schema descriptions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:35) · [Existing outcome keys](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:104)\n\n| Check | What the request still needs to say or encode |\n|---|---|\n| **C1 — source numbers** | A source must supply a shown passage ID and a matching value, unit, bound and component. State the component choices by form. A money range supplies separate `low` and `high` figures, a relative range supplies `midpoint` and `relative`, and a multiplier uses `multiplier` and keeps its qualifier. Ordinary money and percentages use `value`, and qualified figures have specific `bound` rules. The enum names the components without telling the writer when each works. [C1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:78) |\n| **C2 — arithmetic** | State the point-versus-range comparison, exact zero for cancelling terms, allowed rounding, bound direction and what to do with opposing bounds or an unevaluable calculation. Code allows a point at the computed midpoint for most operations, checks both ends for a supplied range and `range_from_relative`, and uses a 0.5% tolerance with floors of 0.05 for percentages and 0.1 otherwise. Bounds can flip on subtraction or division. Opposing directions require an estimate. [Tolerance](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:280) · [Refusals](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:364) |\n| **C3 — part and whole** | Render the actual `compare_periods`. The checker uses each member’s population, measure and scope with each listed period and scenario. It refuses duplicate reachable forecast figures for either side and checks the part against the whole when both exist. It compares corresponding ends for points and closed ranges. With an open bound it asks whether any pair of values can fit. The current general instruction that a part cannot exceed its whole leaves these rules out. [Comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:553) · [Bounds](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:210) |\n| **C4 — shared figures and scenarios** | The exact shared key is all four `what` fields. When an outcome touches that key, every path to it must pass through a forecast figure, with exactly one such figure per represented scenario. A point calculation or estimate cannot borrow a shared forecast or an estimate from another scenario, including through intermediate figures. Part and whole must cover the same estimate-derived scenarios. `range` means an estimate with both ends that serves as an outcome and feeds no figure. The enum alone supplies none of these rules. [Scenario and range checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:512) · [Shared paths](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:572) |\n| **C5 — reference** | A forecast needs exactly one marked reference or a nonempty reason. The rule applies to the entire calculation behind the reference. It must contain at least one external source whose speaker is other than `system`. Every source at the bottom must be external or reported. Estimates, earlier forecasts and figures labelled `forecast` are barred anywhere in the calculation. A direct reported figure alone fails. The individual `basis` and `kind` enums do not encode these combinations. There is no general `basis × kind` cross-check elsewhere beyond the prior rule below. [Choice](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:503) · [Reference graph](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:779) |\n| **C6 — rung** | A rung is an integer from 1 through that member’s ladder length. Its band must **overlap** the recomputed outcome. It can contain just part of a range or bounded outcome. Lower band edges are included and upper edges excluded. If several bands overlap, the reasons should explain the choice, as the original design requires. “The band contains the outcome” reads as full containment. [C6](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:495) · [Band edges](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:200) · [Original design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md:75) |\n| **C7 — structure** | State that all figure links must resolve and none may form a cycle, including through `rests_on`, adjustments and bridges. State exactly one answer per member and the unresolved shape explicitly, including a nonempty reason and no rung. Specify `low ≤ high`, the actual operand limits (`sum` 1–99, `product` and `roll_forward` 2–99, other operations exactly 2), and that null `signs` means all additions. The existing user text covers one answer per member, and the member enum covers unknown member IDs. The repair still needs to define duplicate answer and marker handling. [Figure checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:302) · [Member checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:468) |\n| **C8 — compatible inputs** | Scope the fiscal-period spellings to time aggregation, including same quantity, same fiscal year and disjoint periods that exactly form the result. Name which `sum`/`difference` relations permit differing keys, and that `accounting_parts` needs a caller-declared scope split. The paid builder supplies no `scope_parts`. For `roll_forward`, specify the opening, flows and closing formats. For `overlap_unknown`, the disputed ID must be an actual operand. For `share`, specify one percentage and one whole, whole first. For a bridge, say which operand IDs must match exactly. The current comparison excludes `%` and `x` operands when finding differing keys, and it checks the bridge’s kind and IDs but does not require assumption text. The multiplier exception and per-unit identity need full operand rules. Per-unit `ratio` uses total then price and produces a figure whose measure is `units`. `product` uses a count and price for the same population and scope. The check accepts price in `USD` **or** `USD bn`. [Compatibility](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:398) · [Per-unit identity](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:665) · [Paid family data](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:63) |\n| **C9 and C10 — bases and earlier answers** | C9 requires a value-determining path to the earlier member’s published forecast or the matching scenario behind its range, with no bypass. A citation alone fails, a base that cancels fails, and multiple earlier scenarios must be covered exactly. Code tests dependence by changing the earlier midpoint by 10%. The schema says none of this. C10 and C7’s prior-pointer refusal are closed off in the current wire format by the `kind` and `basis` enums and the absence of `pointer`. Preserve the internal tests for exact member, day and value, comparison-only use, and the ban on using a prior as an outcome or input. [C9 and C10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:599) · [Prior pointer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:357) · [Wire schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:30) |\n\n## Major findings\n\n- **The markers can represent the legitimate old links.** They can mark a range summary as an outcome, let several members share one figure, let a forecast use a computed reference, and represent an unresolved member with neither marker. Define what happens if an unresolved member is marked for a reference or given an unavailable reason. The old checker skipped references for unresolved answers. Also define repeated member IDs on one figure, competing figures, and the treatment of an invalid answer during diagnostic rendering. `from_answer` is a reasonable single place to translate the wire shape. It needs a defined result on marker errors and a path to each raw-answer reader. `Gate.attempt`, `summarise` and `card_lines` each read the raw shape independently. Both scoring and diagnostic packet rendering use `card_lines`. `strict()` is the reverse direction for the render fixture and currently drops fields with new names. [Marker design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:19) · [Unresolved branch](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:484) · [First answer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:165) · [Merge input](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:266) · [Packet input](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:501) · [Fixture encoder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:116)\n\n- **The scenario enum changes what the analyst can express.** `DESIGN.md` allows named scenarios and gives low and high as examples. Two different downside scenarios can have separate assumptions and forecasts. Forcing both into `low` can cause a duplicate-forecast refusal or mix the two calculations. The internal gate even uses `alt` to exercise cross-scenario refusals. Preserve named scenarios, or explicitly account for the narrower contract and prove that it covers the cases this repair is meant to support. [Allowed scenario names](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md:27) · [Alternate scenario fixture](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/gate.py:338)\n\n- **The other §3 changes need sharper controls.** **3.1** adds no acceptance path. A closed list applied to every `what.period` would nevertheless exclude working values such as `rest of FY2027` and `period not specified`. Keep the list local to the operations that parse it. **3.3** would reject a correct calculation I confirmed passes today, `12% × 2x = 24%`. `share` would yield `0.24` with the same operands. The defect is multiplying a whole by a percentage as if the percentage were a raw multiplier. **3.5** excludes the spelling `USD trillion`, but the rung check still accepts `1.05` with an allowed unit and compares the raw number with billion-dollar bands. The enum does not itself verify magnitude or compatibility with the ladder. [Period parser](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:285) · [Working period fixtures](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/gate.py:128) · [Product and share](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:125) · [Rung comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:495)\n\n- **A1 and A2 miss cases that could decide the result.** The stored four-term residual, `$411B − $81.6B − $96.2B − $108B`, still fails C8 as a signed `sum`. I confirmed that omitting the relation fails and `time_aggregation` fails because the annual period overlaps the quarters. `stated_in_addition` passes even though it misdescribes the calculation. For A1, also carry a range outcome with a valid overlapping rung, a shared figure, a computed external reference, an unresolved answer, a roll-forward that records overlap, a valid scope bridge, both per-unit directions and a same-base calculation through the new wire shape. For A2, plant value plus range, a missing range end, duplicate member answers, conflicting reference markers, an outcome key mismatch, a shared-figure bypass, a wrong scenario, a forecast or estimate inside a reference, and a missing or wrong bridge. Test the actual cross-period share assumption too. Correct multiplication does not establish that a Q2 mix applies to a full year. Assert the intended refusal so a schema error cannot mask the check under test. [A1/A2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:115) · [Stored residual](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r48.md:46) · [Sum compatibility](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:407)\n\n- **The six requests test fewer than six independent evidence sets.** The joint pair and both separate requests intentionally share the same evidence. Each reuses **228 of 266** passage IDs from its corresponding paid request and **230 of 266** exact quotes appear somewhere in the paid plan. O reuses **30 of 30**. S has **9 of 50** exact quotes anywhere in the paid plan, including **6 of 50** in its corresponding paid request. E has no valid overlap figure as specified. A genuine Vera candidate, `old-3/9071`, reuses **15 of 15**, while `old-3/8753` reuses **9 of 9** by ID. The high-overlap cases are useful controls for the repair. The test needs a correctly identified request with new decisive evidence to claim it generalizes. Give each writer a fresh context per request. As written, each writer sees the entire batch and can carry its joint answer into the separate requests. [Input list and session setup](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:86) · [Evidence union](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:95)\n\n- **Part B can pass without demonstrating that a writer completed a usable calculation.** I ran an all-unresolved pair through the current checks. It returned zero errors and zero outcomes. Conversely, the design can call even **0 of 12** a clean conformance result if every refusal is attributed to the writer. The **6 of 12** warning has no stated basis and can hide a failure on every joint request. Register the forms each case can genuinely exercise, report supported forecasts, justified unresolved answers and refusals separately, and require successful coverage of the joint and singleton forms before calling the test clean. Have independent readers who did not write the design or the answers record two separate facts for each refusal: whether the exact outgoing request states the condition, and whether the answer is correct against the shown passages and governing design. Both problems can occur together. Resolve disagreements before declaring a pass. Classify truncation, session failure and checker exceptions separately from writer mistakes. Stronger writers can demonstrate that they can follow a single outgoing request. At $0, replay the observed Luna mistake patterns from both journals against the new schema and check that each is prevented or gets a clear reason, then compare strong writers on the old and repaired requests in separate contexts. Actual Luna compliance remains unmeasured. [Classification and stop rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:139) · [Unresolved branch](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:479) · [Stored failure census](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE-RESULT.md:25)\n\n## Build and record\n\n- **The rehearsal must read the new plan, and the old run must keep its reader.** The rehearsal loads `paid-plan.json` at import and validates outgoing bytes against that object. Updating stubs alone still rehearses the old schema. The equivalent repair run should consume a separately pinned plan and compare it with the old plan by case, evidence, questions, family data and intended request changes. The old journals store the raw old shape. Replacing `strip` everywhere would reinterpret those entries during packet rendering and recovery. Recovery also rewrites `results.json`. Bind decoding and checking to the plan version and verify historical reproduction on a copy. I confirmed the current plan hash matches its pin, the run’s plan has identical data, and the current builder recreates the exact original plan bytes. [Rehearsal plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_rehearsal.py:18) · [Byte comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_rehearsal.py:120) · [Recovery and send pin](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:365)\n\n- **9,624 characters is one old schema’s size.** Across the 12 stored cases, schemas were **5,652–10,056 characters** and user messages **13,202–134,199 characters**. The 36 scored calls used **5,534–38,797 input tokens** each. Copying the evidence enum adds up to about **2,332 serialized characters** before new descriptions, and the enum already appears in `cites` and `pushes`. Use one schema definition for passage IDs if the strict request path accepts it. Report whole-request characters, estimated tokens and maximum size before and after. Write the actual field descriptions into the design for review now. Keep the paid examples as tests and use examples from other domains in the request. [Size proposal](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:167) · [Repeated passage enum](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:61) · [Prompt size rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:220)\n\n**Recommendation:** bring back one revised design with the exact schema wording and corrected case list. The decisive $0 test is to send the registered good and bad forms through the same schema, converter and checks the gate uses, then read the blind writers’ first answers against those same rules and passages.**Round 51 found serious issues. Fix them before round 52.** The clearest example is the Vera CPU control. Its source says NVIDIA “not only still expects $20 billion.” The proposed three-word negation rule can reject the very number that control needs. The blind test also leaves a gap in the other direction. The checker accepted an unsupported forecast in a read-only probe, and §5 explicitly assigns the independent readers only the refused answers. [Repair design §3.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:109) · [Vera control](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/gate.py:182) · [Blind reading protocol](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:215)\n\nI matched the system text, user text and schema against all 72 saved requests, including retry messages, and reproduced all 72 refusal lists. The counterexamples to proposed changes below are deductions from the design, with current checker behavior tested in memory where applicable. No files were changed and no model requests were sent. [Sent plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan.json) · [First answers](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/answers.jsonl) · [Retries](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/retries.jsonl)\n\n## 1. Coverage\n\nThe table accounts for all 58 current refusal templates and the proposed changes that add or alter refusals.\n\n| Check | Where §2 states it and what is still missing |\n|---|---|\n| **C1 · 3 templates** | `evidence_id` covers an unshown ID through the enum. A source can still supply `null`, so say its ID is required. `expression` covers an unmatched span, and `component`, `unit` and `bound` cover value, unit and qualifier mismatches. The text implies that every complete number and qualifier in a quote can be copied. The extractor accepts specific forms. For example, it takes `$108 billion, plus or minus 2%` from the new pair’s quote even though the quote says **approximately** before it. State which surrounding words are excluded, how trailing qualifiers map to `component`, and exactly what the new negation refusal covers. [Wording](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:67) · [C1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:78) |\n| **C2 · 6 templates, plus §3.3** | `operation` covers wrong arithmetic, the tolerance and the money-by-percent ban. `bound` partly covers wrong declared bounds and bounds declared on point inputs. Missing are unevaluable arithmetic, such as division by zero, exact zero when operands cancel, and refusal when the derived bounds oppose each other. The current explicit-bound check compares **direction**, so `>=` passes for a derived `>` and is subsequently replaced. “Must match” must say whether it means direction or exact qualifier. C2 also accepts the midpoint of a computed interval for most operations when the answer declares a point. The instruction that a computed range always states both ends is stricter. [Wording](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:67) · [C2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:364) |\n| **C3 · 2 templates** | The family header covers the listed periods and the general part-versus-whole rule. It leaves out the duplicate-forecast refusal. The checker walks from each member’s outcome to same-key forecasts, separately for each named period and scenario. More than one matching forecast on either side is refused. If either side has none, the comparison is skipped. For points and closed ranges, compare corresponding ends. With a one-sided bound on either side, refuse only if **no allowed pair** fits. A part `>120` and whole `≤120` fail, while `≥120` and `≤120` fit at 120. [Header](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:94) · [Bound comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:210) · [Forecast lookup](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:553) |\n| **C4 · 7 templates** | `scenario` covers cross-scenario estimates, equal scenario sets for a part and its whole, and the range summary’s shape and no-reader rule. Say that the checker derives those sets from upstream **estimate** figures. `basis` and the shared-quantity header cover missing and duplicate shared forecasts, borrowing from another scenario, and bypassing the shared forecast. The scope is off. The shared rule starts when an **outcome** reaches the quantity. Every path from that outcome to a matching figure must meet a forecast first. A guide or consensus can feed the forecast. The wording currently reads as if the guide must go through the forecast itself. The separate cross-scenario forecast check applies to **shared** forecasts, while §2 bans all cross-scenario forecast dependencies. [Basis and scenario](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:62) · [Scenario checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:512) · [Shared paths](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:572) |\n| **C5 · 6 templates, plus markers** | `reference_for`, `shape` and `reference_unavailable` cover the exclusive choice, nonempty reason, forecast/estimate ban and allowed source bases. Marking the figure itself removes the old dangling reference pointer. The walk includes the marked figure and all its upstream figures. At least one source leaf must have an external basis **and a passage speaker other than `system`**. The code still accepts a second `system`-speaker leaf with an external basis. I confirmed that combination passes. Also, nullable evidence on a source in this graph can raise `KeyError` after C1 has already identified the missing evidence. The old “leaf neither external nor reported” template is covered by the basis enum and the forecast ban. [Reference wording](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:83) · [Choice](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:503) · [Leaf walk](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:779) |\n| **C6 · 2 templates, plus §3.7** | `rung` and its integer schema cover validity and band overlap. `unit` and the header cover the proposed member-unit check. The overlap uses the **recomputed** outcome. A band includes its lower edge and excludes its upper edge. The outcome’s endpoints matter too. For a band starting at 120, `<120` fails and `≤120` passes at exactly 120. `approx_below` also includes its endpoint in code, `approx_above` includes its lower endpoint, and `approx` alone is treated as a point. §2 gives ordinary meanings for those words without stating these consequences. [Rung wording](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:90) · [Value sets and band edges](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:182) · [Rung check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:492) |\n| **C7 · 14 templates, plus §3.6 and markers** | `id`, `value`/`low`/`high`, `figures`, `operation` and `signs` cover duplicate IDs, numeric shape, cycles, arity and signs. The kind, basis and operation enums cover their closed sets. The ID descriptions cover dangling links, though `rests_on` should say explicitly that its entries must resolve to a defined figure or a shown passage. The member enum and existing one-answer-per-member footer cover unknown, omitted and doubled answers. `shape`, `why` and `outcome_for` cover unresolved answers, missing outcomes and wrong outcome keys. §1 says a member cannot repeat on one outcome marker list, but §2 never says so. It also leaves repeated reference markers on the same figure ambiguous. §2 states the proposed source-with-forecast-basis refusal. A missing prior pointer is unreachable through the wire schema. [Marker contract](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:25) · [Footer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:109) · [Structure](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:302) · [Answer ownership](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:468) |\n| **C8 · 8 templates** | `relation` and `disputed_input_id` cover time aggregation, both disputed-input messages, the missing declared split and the missing relation for a sum or difference. The time-aggregation sentence needs to require the fiscal spellings when this operation parses them. `roll_forward` omits the required closing-period spelling. It also says flows must be later, while the check only looks at the period labels. `share` gives the formula without stating the refusal for anything other than exactly one percentage operand. `bridge_estimate_id` and `converts_input_ids` largely cover a missing or wrong bridge. However, C8 compares a set of IDs and checks the bridge’s kind. It does not validate the assumption text or whether a `stated_in_addition` passage really supports addition. For the per-unit exception, specify **exactly two operands**, total first and price second for division, same population and scope, and the billion-to-dollar conversion. The multiplier exception requires at least one `x` input and the other inputs to match population, measure and scope. It can cross periods, and a valid `12% × 2x` needs to be explicit. The `apply_growth` exception in code is broader than the wording. Any `same_base` relation in the family can activate it for matching scope. [Operation and relation wording](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:73) · [Arithmetic scaling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:134) · [C8](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:398) · [Per-unit identity](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:665) |\n| **C9 · 6 templates** | The same-base header partly covers using the earlier forecast, failing to reach it, and bypassing it. It does not state that each later forecast must use the earlier one through **calculation inputs**, that a range’s earlier scenario forecasts must be directly named in `rests_on`, that multiple earlier scenarios must match the later set, or that a range which only cites the earlier forecast fails. Most importantly, the calculation must respond when the earlier forecast changes. The existing plant `consensus + base − base` reaches the base and still fails because moving it changes nothing. The checker probes a 10% midpoint change. State the value-dependence requirement beside the family relation. [Header](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:94) · [C9](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:599) · [Cancellation plant](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/gate.py:476) |\n| **C10 · 4 templates** | The wire format excludes `prior`, `prior_forecast` and the pointer. This makes all four prior-figure refusals unreachable for a schema-valid answer. [Wire schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:30) · [C10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:642) |\n\n## 2. Wording\n\n- **The negation sentence changes the source’s role.** “State it as an estimate” can turn a company’s qualified guidance into the analyst’s own judgement. The rule for representing a source should say when a quote cannot be encoded as a source figure. The analyst can still cite it as context. An estimate should reflect an actual judgement. The example “a fall of 12% = -12” also conflicts with the proposed extractor, which only preserves a literal leading minus. [Unit and expression wording](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:68) · [Governing answer design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md:67)\n- **“A shown passage says the amounts add” is supported by the design, but the relation label alone passes the checker.** Round 50’s example still works. A total plus its own segment can pass when the writer declares `stated_in_addition`. Put that exact case in the human reading, including when the checker accepts the answer. The human also needs to distinguish valid arithmetic from an unsupported assumption that a quarter’s mix applies to the full year. Neither requires a new judging rule. [Relation wording](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:75) · [C8 relation branch](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:407)\n- **The §2 examples name no covered company or product.** The money and percentage examples are generic. The exception to the gate-example rule is the exact worked phrase **“more than double” → `>2x`**, which is the decisive expression in Vera control R4. Keep the supported multiplier words in the syntax and use “more than triple” as the worked example. The actual archived figures in §5 belong in the test. [Examples](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:68) · [R4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/gate.py:182)\n\n## 3. Counterexamples to §3\n\n| Change | Decisive counterexample |\n|---|---|\n| **3.1 · Signed periods** | `FY − Q1 reported + a different Q1 estimate = FY` passes the signed quarter counts. The two Q1 figures can differ, so the result is a revised forecast disguised as a time aggregation. The net counts alone cannot support the promise that overlapping inputs are refused. Keep the valid `FY − Q1 − Q2 − Q3 = Q4` control alongside a case with opposing signs on **different** figures for one quarter. [Proposed count](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:106) |\n| **3.3 · Product** | `100 units × 12% = 1,200 units` passed today. The proposed money-only guard still permits it. The correct share is 12 units. Keep `12% × 2x = 24%` as the positive control so the fix preserves multiplier arithmetic. [Proposed guard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:108) · [Product implementation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:134) |\n| **3.4 · Sign, trailing qualifier and negation** | For sign, test both `-12%` and `−12%`, and distinguish them from `a fall of 12%`, which the wording currently promises to read as negative. For a trailing qualifier, `\"$5 billion, or less\"` must preserve `≤` through the comma. For negation, `\"not only $20 billion in sales, but also …\"` affirms the amount and a word window rejects it. Conversely, `\"does not in any plausible scenario expect to exceed $5 billion\"` reaches past that window. E’s actual `\"not only still expects $20 billion\"` makes the word-count boundary consequential. [Proposed extraction change](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:109) · [Extractor patterns](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:12) |\n| **3.5 · Null bound** | Let `A = >10 + 5` and `B = A + <8`, both with null declared bounds. If the repair only allows null in the current C2 pass, B sees a point A during validation and misses the opposing bounds. I confirmed the existing recomputation then derives `mixed` for B, which overlaps any rung. Validate against the same derived bounds used for publication. Test the two-step chain, an explicit wrong bound, and the valid one-step omission. [Current validation order](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:371) · [Recomputation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:457) |\n| **3.6 · Source basis** | A source labelled `guidance` can be marked as both the forecast outcome and the reference. I confirmed the equivalent internal answer passes and publishes. The new check only rejects a source labelled `forecast`. Resolve explicitly whether an outside figure can itself be marked as the family forecast, so the marker description and check give the same answer. [Proposed refusal](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:111) · [Outcome validation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:488) |\n| **3.7 · Outcome units** | A trillions figure written as `1.05` with the allowed label `USD bn` still passes the unit check and can select a low rung. A separate in-memory probe also passed a same-key one-input sum that copied a `USD` input unchanged into a `USD bn` outcome. The new equality check protects the outcome’s **label**. Register the correct `1050 USD bn` normalization and have the readers check scale against the quote. [Proposed unit check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:112) · [Sum and rung checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:407) |\n\n## 4. Registered cases and what they can decide\n\nI verified the archive headings against their stored questions and ladders. The figures below are the dividing points in rung order, in billions of dollars. The counts of quotes absent from the paid plan are correct. §5 should pin the actual ladders and units, since its current build requirement checks only the thesis ID and question. [Registered list](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:145) · [Ladder lookup](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:49)\n\n| Case | Verified input | Registration issue |\n|---|---|---|\n| **P and the two separate calls** | `old-1/8810 v4`, FY2027 company revenue, descending **431.2, 392, 352.8, 313.6**. `old-1/8816 v8`, FY2027 Data Center revenue, descending **400, 350, 300, 250**. **296** passages and **79** new exact quotes. | New wording in a quote can repeat an old fact. For example, new `e4899` gives the same **$108B ±2%** guidance as old `e2499`. If the test is meant to exercise fresh evidence that changes a calculation, name the passage and the changed input beforehand. |\n| **S** | `old-3/9043 v6`, four hyperscalers’ data-center capex in **CY2026**, ascending **500, 600, 700, 800**. **50** passages and **41** new exact quotes. | `e2458` supplies four-company capex at $760B. `e4766` supplies five-company data-center capex near $800B. Those are useful fresh inputs for a scope conversion. A supported estimate can also reach the band without a computed bridge. Define which answer forms count, and use A1 to guarantee the bridge itself is exercised. |\n| **O** | `old-2/8507 v29`, commitments **at publication of the FY2027 annual report**, ascending **25, 50, 75, 100**. **30** passages and **0** new quotes. Both overlap sources are present. | `end of FY2027` is the existing harness key. The archived question names the report’s publication. Record explicitly that the balance is the fiscal-close figure reported at publication if that is the intended quantity. Otherwise the instructions point to two dates. |\n| **E** | `old-3/9071 v41`, FY2028 Vera CPU revenue, descending **50, 40, 30, 20**. **15** passages and **0** new quotes. `e3660` supplies both the $20B CPU base and the multiplier. | Pin the positive extraction of both expressions and keep the CPU-to-Vera assumption visible. |\n\n**A1 is expressible if it uses its own registered fixtures.** The shared-outcome example requires two members with the same `what` and compatible ladders. Neither pair member can share the other’s outcome in P. The same-base example also needs its own family because none of the six blind requests declares that relation. Both per-unit directions fit as intermediate calculations, with the money forecast as the member outcome. The null-bound form fits the schema, subject to the validation issue above. The Vera source control is expressible as JSON but can be refused by the proposed negation rule. [A1 list](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:158) · [Pair declaration](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:63) · [Existing same-base fixture](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/gate.py:261)\n\n**A2 and A3 are incomplete.** For A2, the decisive additions are a plain wrong result and an unevaluable operation, a C3 closed-range and open-bound edge pair, the C6 edge pair, C9 cancellation, a value with just one range end, a missing reference choice, a repeated marker on one figure, and the chained null-bound case. The existing `value plus range` plant misses `value plus just low`, which I confirmed passes C7. For A3, both journals add concrete cases absent from the list, including `range_from_relative` with one input, a qualified computed result declared as a point, and `overlap_unknown` without its disputed operand. Retain the exact journal examples and assert the specific refusal or accepted correction. [A2/A3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:178) · [First-answer arity errors](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/answers.jsonl) · [Bound retry](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/retries.jsonl:6) · [Overlap retry](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/retries.jsonl:44)\n\n## 5. What must be settled before the blind test\n\n1. **Critical — agree how an accepted answer earns “supported.”** Have both readers grade accepted first answers against the shown passages as well as reviewing refusals. Record whether the calculation passes, whether the forecast is supported, and whether the existing publication check would hold the family. Count a usable joint reply only when both forecasts are supported in that same publishable reply. This closes the actual gap in the pass decision. [Reader and stop rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:219) · [Existing publication check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:165)\n2. **High — settle the quote and bound counterexamples and the incomplete instructions.** E’s affirmative source, the chained opposing bounds, C3/C6 equality, C5 source attribution, and C9 cancellation each need a fixed correct case and a broken counterpart. The old harness can confirm existing behavior. Round 52 must show that the new outgoing wording and checker agree on those same cases. [Proposed check changes](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REPAIR-DESIGN.md:102) · [Round 50 finish line](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r50.md)\n\nUse the remaining round to verify those registered cases through the exact request and checks the harness uses. If a serious issue remains, return it to Alex under the round 50 finish line.   140\t- Expected growth is about 6,000–10,000 characters of schema descriptions (round 50's estimate is a largest schema of 16,000–20,000).\n   141\t- The written reason (AGENTS §6): these are the definitions the checks already enforce.\n   142\t- The passage-id enum appears three times: `evidence_id`, `cites` and `pushes`. One `$defs` entry is used if `model.check_schema` and\n   143\t  the provider's strict mode accept `$ref`. Otherwise it stays repeated, and its size is reported.\n   144\t\n   145\t## 5. The blind conformance test (registered here; $0, no provider call)\n   146\t\n   147\t**Inputs**, built by the repaired `paid_gate.item`. Each case's archive, call id, question, period, ladder and unit are registered\n   148\ttogether, and the build refuses a heading whose thesis id or question differs.\n   149\t\n   150\t| Case | Archive / call | Member key | Evidence | Role |\n   151\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n   152\t| P (joint) | old-1 v4 8810 + v8 8816 | NVIDIA revenue company FY2027; NVIDIA revenue Data Center FY2027 | union 296 passages, 79 quotes absent from the gate's plan | fresh evidence; the pair shape |\n   153\t| P-v4, P-v8 (separate) | the same calls, one header each | as above | the same union | the separate shape |\n   154\t| S | old-3 v6 9043 | four largest AI hyperscalers, data-center capex, combined, **CY2026** | 50 passages, 41 fresh | fresh evidence; a scope bridge |\n   155\t| O | old-2 v29 8507 | NVIDIA equity investment commitments company end of FY2027 | 30, none fresh | control: roll_forward with overlap |\n   156\t| E | old-3 v41 9071 | NVIDIA revenue Vera CPU FY2028 | 15, none fresh | control: multiplier and adjustment |\n   157\t\n   158\t**Part A, the checks against registered forms** (code; each asserts its intended check and message, and a schema error cannot mask it).\n   159\t\n   160\t- **A1, correct forms in v13r.** Each must pass:\n   161\t  - $108.0B ± 2% as midpoint and relative, with range_from_relative;\n   162\t  - Q1 + Q2 = FY2027 H1;\n   163\t  - FY − Q1 − Q2 − Q3 = Q4 as a signed time_aggregation;\n   164\t  - a year-over-year rate on the prior-year quarter, with a bridge;\n   165\t  - a whole × mix via share;\n   166\t  - \"over $300 billion\" (from \"well over $300 billion\") and \"65%\" as exact spans;\n   167\t  - $1.05 trillion as 1050 USD bn;\n   168\t  - a range outcome whose rung overlaps it;\n   169\t  - one figure marked for two members;\n   170\t  - a computed external reference (consensus × reported mix);\n   171\t  - an unresolved member with nothing marked;\n   172\t  - a roll_forward with an overlap recorded;\n   173\t  - a valid scope bridge;\n   174\t  - both per-unit directions;\n   175\t  - a same-base family computing from the earlier forecast;\n   176\t  - 12% × 2x = 24%;\n   177\t  - a computed figure with its bound left null.\n   178\t- **A2, planted defects on copies of A1.** Each is refused by its named check:\n   179\t  - 108.5 for $108.0B (C1);\n   180\t  - \"$300 billion\" stripped of its qualifier (C1);\n   181\t  - \"-12%\" taken as 12 (C1);\n   182\t  - \"$300 million or more\" taken as a point (C1);\n   183\t  - \"not be over $300 billion\" as a source (C1);\n   184\t  - value plus range (C7);\n   185\t  - a missing range end (C7);\n   186\t  - Q2 + Q3 labelled H1 (C8);\n   187\t  - a Data Center quarter added into company revenue with no relation (C8);\n   188\t  - money × % through product (C2);\n   189\t  - a rate on another period's base with no bridge (C8);\n   190\t  - a cycle (C7);\n   191\t  - no outcome marker, two outcome markers, and a marker on an unresolved member (C7);\n   192\t  - both a reference marker and a reason (C5);\n   193\t  - a forecast inside a reference (C5);\n   194\t  - an outcome key mismatch (C7);\n   195\t  - a shared-quarter bypass (C4);\n   196\t  - a cross-scenario estimate (C4);\n   197\t  - a bridge converting the wrong inputs (C8);\n   198\t  - an outcome in the wrong unit (C6);\n   199\t  - a source labelled forecast (C7);\n   200\t  - duplicate member answers (C7).\n   201\t- **A3, Luna's observed mistakes** (from both journals). Each is encoded on the v13r shape and is either impossible under the\n   202\t  schema (an enum) or refused with a reason the request states (the sentence is quoted):\n   203\t  - prose outcome, reference, evidence and bridge;\n   204\t  - unit spellings;\n   205\t  - value with range;\n   206\t  - signs on a difference;\n   207\t  - a four-input difference;\n   208\t  - money × % via product;\n   209\t  - \"first half\";\n   210\t  - \"65% growth in Q4\";\n   211\t  - a passage id in inputs and in adjusts;\n   212\t  - a trillion outcome.\n   213\t- **A4, the existing harness.** The $0 gate, the rehearsal and the mutants pass, and the old run reproduces.\n   214\t\n   215\t**Part B, blind writers.**\n   216\t- **Two writers:** Claude subagents and fresh read-only Codex sessions. Each writer works in a fresh context per case (12 sessions).\n   217\t  Each gets only that case's exact outgoing system text, user text and schema, and the instruction to answer as the JSON schema\n   218\t  defines it.\n   219\t- **The first outputs** go through `model.check_schema`, `from_answer` and `check` unedited.\n   220\t- **Two readers** who wrote neither the design nor the answers (a Claude subagent and a Codex session) record two facts for each\n   221\t  refusal:\n   222\t  - whether the exact outgoing request states the condition, quoting the sentence;\n   223\t  - whether the answer is correct against the shown passages.\n   224\t- **A third reader** settles disagreements. Truncation, session failures and checker exceptions are classed apart.\n   225\t- **Reported:** per case, supported forecasts, justified unresolved answers, and refusals by rule.\n   226\t\n   227\t**Stop.** The test stops on any of these:\n   228\t- an A1 form refused;\n   229\t- an A2 defect escaping its intended check;\n   230\t- an A3 mistake neither impossible nor stated;\n   231\t- a Part B refusal whose condition the request does not state, or that refuses a correct answer;\n   232\t- an INCOMPLETE run;\n   233\t- a case registered as answerable (P, P-v4, P-v8, S, E, O) with zero usable first replies across both writers;\n   234\t- the joint case without both supported forecasts in one reply.\n   235\t\n   236\t**A clean result** goes to Alex as a request for the paid comparison: the same 36 requests rebuilt with v13r, under a new decision\n   237\twith D725's lines. Only that run measures whether Luna can do this at medium effort in one pass.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; sed -n '11210,11285p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n   word for it is already given.\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\n\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\nany one step's own score.\n\n## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n\n**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n\nThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n\n- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\n- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\n  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \"below $40 billion\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\n  nothing at all and were never judged.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n| Evidence | Content | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Filing recognises only \"its own figure\" | The model says \"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\" and \"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\n| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \"below $40 billion\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\n| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \"What it does not measure\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\n| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\n\nAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\n\n## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n\n| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \"好，删掉卡片代码\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\n| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \"supports\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \"whose conclusion to read\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \"total revenue × 92%\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \"supports\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\n| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\"keep only the narrowest question\" takes a seed arrow for \"a narrower sub-question\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\n| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\n| One general sentence, \"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\n| Tightening D259's \"leeway\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\n| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\n\n## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\n\n- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\n  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\n  system (D263).\n- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\n  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\n  work (2026-11-04: \"好你去解决问题\", \"开始做\"); making it the default needs his word again.\n- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\n- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\n  each one at evaluation\"; §5.1, \"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\", with four paths, \"demand, supply, competition, pricing\"; §5.3,\n  \"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\n  competition or pricing\".\n- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\n  \"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \"bounded by\n  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\n  of the previous filing topic).\n- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\n  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\n  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\n  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\n- **Code decides only \"is it the same thing\", never \"does it matter\"** (AGENTS §2).\n\n## 5. What to do\n\nStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\n\n1. **Replace the abstract sentence \"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\n   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\n   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\n   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\n     the existing rule).\n   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\n   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\n   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\n   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\n     sales and share, for the question they affect.\n2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\n   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\n   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\n   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\n   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\n   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\n   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \"when the other\n   party's question is open … file it there as well\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\n3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \"no home\" and\n   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\n4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\n   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\n\n## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\n\n- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\n  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\n  keys were sorted alphabetically.\n- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\n  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\n  measured and reported apart.\n- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\n- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \"keep only the narrowest\" and \"no home means dropped\"), and is\n  counted after.\n- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\n  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \"optional\" counts as\n  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\n  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \"fact ×\n    question\";\n  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\n  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\n  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\n    or no question uses);\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\n    ones that matter one by one.\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \"every draw above the highest of the control's\n  three\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\n      facts must not fall.\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \"one fewer\" for that\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \"lost outright\". A move to another question\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\n      question counts. \"One more\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\n      control never does counts as \"new noise\"; filed all three times, it counts as \"outright new noise\". The opposite direction offsets it.\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\n      smallest values that keep \"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\n      what was measured.\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n\n## 7. Process (no drift)\n\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n  sentence, in both directions.\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n\n## 8. Steps and where we are\n\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n\n- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n## D736 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 51: the repair's wording review finds as many serious issues as round 49; Claude and Codex split on going back to Alex now\n\n- **Round 51** (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r51.md`) reviewed design v2's exact wording and cases. It reproduced all 72\n  stored refusals and found these serious issues:\n  - **Still unstated:** rules in C1 to C9, among them C3's duplicate-forecast and open-bound rules, C4's outcome-scoped path rule,\n    C5's speaker condition, C6's band and endpoint semantics, C8's per-unit and multiplier operand rules, and C9's value-dependence\n    test.\n  - **Counterexamples to every proposed check change:**\n    - the negation window refuses E's own source, \"not only still expects $20 billion\";\n    - signed period sets pass a revised forecast disguised as an aggregation;\n    - \"100 units × 12% = 1,200 units\" passes the product guard;\n    - a chained null bound hides opposing bounds;\n    - an outside guidance figure can be marked as both the forecast and the reference.\n  - **Gaps in the test:**\n    - the blind readers judged only refused answers, so an accepted but unsupported forecast would count as usable;\n    - A2 and A3 miss decisive cases.\n- **The pattern:** rounds 48, 49 and 51 each found many serious issues of one mechanism: the checks enforce more rules than a request\n  can state for a one-pass model. AGENTS §1 says: \"When one mechanism draws findings round after round, stop answering findings:\n  propose one structural rule.\"\n- **Positions:**\n  - **Codex:** fix the round-51 issues, use the second allowed round (D735) on the sent request and checks, and return to Alex only\n    if a serious issue remains.\n  - **Claude:** go back to Alex now. Round 51's evidence came after D735's consensus. Shrinking the checks is the structural rule,\n    and it is his to choose, because it exceeds D734.\n  - Alex is active, so the choice goes to him with both positions.\n\n## D737 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: shrink judging-v13's format to the checks that stop the named defects, then a $0 blind test\n\n- **The question** (after D736): \"判数字新版本的修补连续三轮审查都在冒新规则（填写说明将从 1 万字涨到约 2 万字，每个答案约 16 个数、每个数要同时满足几十条规则）。Codex 主张修完再审最后一轮；我主张现在改结构。下一步怎么走？\"\n  Options:\n  - 砍成小格式再盲测 (recommended): keep only the checks that stop five defects (a number misread, wrong arithmetic, a part\n    above its whole or added into it, two forecasts of one quarter, an own estimate passed off as the market's); the other rules\n    become assumptions shown to readers; council, then the $0 blind test, then a request for the paid re-send;\n  - 按原计划再修一轮 (Codex's position);\n  - 关掉这条线.\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-22), the recommended option (\"…成小格式再盲测 (推荐)\").\n- **Decided (Alex):**\n  - The judging-v13 format shrinks. Code refuses an answer only for the five defects above and for broken structure (links that do\n    not resolve, a cycle, a missing or doubled answer, an outcome not of the question's quantity, a rung that does not hold the\n    outcome).\n  - Each such rule is written in one or two sentences beside its field. Every other rule of DESIGN.md's checks becomes an assumption\n    recorded and shown to the readers, never a refusal.\n  - The council reviews within that scope. A counterexample that lets none of the five defects through is a reader's matter, not a\n    finding.\n  - Then the $0 blind test (REPAIR-DESIGN.md §5, with round 51's reader fix). A clean result returns to Alex for the paid re-send under\n    D725's lines.\n- **Superseded:** REPAIR-DESIGN.md v2's full restatement (D735's finish line), replaced by the small format.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
