{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'consensus of \\\\\"'$480 billion|Second-quarter revenue hit '\"\\\\\"'$96.2bn|Data centre revenue more than doubled|roughly twice as many chips|US'\"\\\\\"'$3.5 billion|a (decline|drop|fall) of [0-9.]+%|fell [0-9.]+%'\"' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan.json -m 14 -o; rg -n 'def check_schema|def _schema' src/hivemind/model.py; rg -n '\"'^[[:space:]]*def |q3-unit|dc-q4-dup'\"' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_rehearsal.py; tail -65 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py | sed -n '182,215p;554,599p;675,690p;730,743p'\"","aggregated_output":"11:Second-quarter revenue hit $96.2bn\n11:Data centre revenue more than doubled\n1679:Second-quarter revenue hit $96.2bn\n1683:Data centre revenue more than doubled\n2406:Second-quarter revenue hit $96.2bn\n2519:Data centre revenue more than doubled\n2544:Second-quarter revenue hit $96.2bn\n2544:Data centre revenue more than doubled\n4171:Second-quarter revenue hit $96.2bn\n4175:Data centre revenue more than doubled\n4888:Second-quarter revenue hit $96.2bn\n5001:Data centre revenue more than doubled\n5026:Second-quarter revenue hit $96.2bn\n5026:Data centre revenue more than doubled\n6653:Second-quarter revenue hit $96.2bn\n6657:Data centre revenue more than doubled\n7370:Second-quarter revenue hit $96.2bn\n184:def check_schema(value, schema, path='$', root=None):\n24:    def __init__(self, body):\n27:    def read(self):\n30:    def __enter__(self):\n33:    def __exit__(self, *exc):\n37:def mid(band):\n42:def valid_answer(it, flavour='ok'):\n55:        if flavour in ('q3-agree', 'q3-disagree', 'q3-float', 'q3-unit') and shared:\n60:            q3_unit = 'USD' if (flavour == 'q3-unit' and m['what']['scope'] == 'Data Center') else 'USD bn'   # [47e.2] the same number, another unit\n71:        if flavour == 'dc-q4-dup' and m['what']['scope'] == 'Data Center':   # [47c.1] two equal forecasts of one quarter in one answer\n112:def http_error(url, code):\n117:    def __init__(self, cfg, scenario, ledger):\n120:    def expected(self, it, user):\n126:    def __call__(self, http_request, *args, **kwargs):\n150:            flavour = {'separate-agree': 'q3-agree', 'separate-disagree': 'q3-disagree', 'separate-agree-float': 'q3-float', 'separate-unit': 'q3-unit'}[s]\n152:            flavour = 'dc-q4-dup'\n195:def scenario(scratch, name, ceiling=0.5, interrupted=False):\n230:def main(scratch):\n234:    def check(name, ok, detail=''):\n265:    def card(usable='yes', gap='no', drop=None, b_differs=None, third=None):\n266:        def one():\n279:    def readings(good_separate, defect_arm=None, drop_packet=False, bad_card=False, missing_ground=False, disagree=None, null_ground=False,\n306:    def verdict_of(rd, name, out=None, keys=None, packets_sha=None):\n451:    def read_all(folder, keys):\n  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\n  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\n    or no question uses);\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\n    ones that matter one by one.\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \"every draw above the highest of the control's\n  three\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\n      facts must not fall.\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \"one fewer\" for that\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \"lost outright\". A move to another question\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\n      question counts. \"One more\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\n      control never does counts as \"new noise\"; filed all three times, it counts as \"outright new noise\". The opposite direction offsets it.\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\n      smallest values that keep \"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\n      what was measured.\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n\n## 7. Process (no drift)\n\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n  sentence, in both directions.\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n\n## 8. Steps and where we are\n\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n\n- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n   182\tdef _outcome_set(fig):\n   183\t    \"\"\"The values an outcome allows: (low, low_closed, high, high_closed); a bound keeps its side open or closed.\"\"\"\n   184\t    lo, hi = _interval(fig)\n   185\t    b = fig.get('bound')\n   186\t    inf = float('inf')\n   187\t    if b == '>':\n   188\t        return (lo, False, inf, False)\n   189\t    if b in ('>=', 'approx_above'):\n   190\t        return (lo, True, inf, False)\n   191\t    if b == '<':\n   192\t        return (-inf, False, hi, False)\n   193\t    if b in ('<=', 'approx_below'):\n   194\t        return (-inf, False, hi, True)\n   195\t    if b == 'mixed':                                    # [46v] any value: only possible crossings\n   196\t        return (-inf, False, inf, False)\n   197\t    return (lo, True, hi, True)\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\tdef _overlaps(values, band):\n   201\t    \"\"\"A band [low, high) (None: open-ended) shares at least one value with the outcome's set.\"\"\"\n   202\t    lo, lo_c, hi, hi_c = values\n   203\t    b_lo = band[0] if band[0] is not None else float('-inf')\n   204\t    b_hi = band[1] if band[1] is not None else float('inf')\n   205\t    low, low_closed = (lo, lo_c) if lo > b_lo else ((b_lo, True) if b_lo > lo else (lo, lo_c))\n   206\t    high, high_closed = (hi, hi_c) if hi < b_hi else ((b_hi, False) if b_hi < hi else (hi, False))\n   207\t    return low < high or (low == high and low_closed and high_closed)\n   208\t\n   209\t\n   210\tdef _exceeds(part, whole):\n   211\t    \"\"\"[46t.2] With a bound on either side, the part exceeds its whole only when no pair of allowed values fits (part min above whole\n   212\t    max). Closed ranges and points keep the paired-end rule (each end of the part at most the same end of the whole).\"\"\"\n   213\t    (plo, plc, phi, phc), (wlo, wlc, whi, whc) = part, whole\n   214\t    inf = float('inf')\n   215\t    if inf in (abs(plo), abs(phi), abs(wlo), abs(whi)):\n   554\t    for rel in family.get('relations', []):\n   555\t        if rel['type'] != 'part_of' or rel['part'] not in outcomes or rel['whole'] not in outcomes:\n   556\t            continue\n   557\t        part_m, whole_m = members[rel['part']], members[rel['whole']]\n   558\t        for sc in scenarios:\n   559\t            for period in family.get('compare_periods', []):\n   560\t                def node(view_id, member):\n   561\t                    want = (member['what']['population'], member['what']['measure'], member['what']['scope'], period)\n   562\t                    hits = sorted((figs[f] for f in reachable(outcomes[view_id]) if _key(figs[f]['what']) == want\n   563\t                                   and figs[f]['basis'] == 'forecast' and figs[f].get('scenario', 'base') == sc), key=lambda f: f['id'])\n   564\t                    if len(hits) > 1:                 # [46x.1] one forecast per member quantity, period and scenario\n   565\t                        errors.append(('C3', f'{period} {sc}: {view_id} has {len(hits)} forecasts ({\", \".join(f[\"id\"] for f in hits)}); '\n   566\t                                             'the comparison is ambiguous'))\n   567\t                        return None\n   568\t                    return hits[0] if hits else None\n   569\t                p, w = node(rel['part'], part_m), node(rel['whole'], whole_m)\n   570\t                if p and w and _exceeds(_outcome_set(p), _outcome_set(w)):          # [46s] open and closed ends kept\n   571\t                    errors.append(('C3', f'{period} {sc}: {rel[\"part\"]} {p[\"id\"]} {_outcome_set(p)} exceeds {rel[\"whole\"]} {w[\"id\"]} {_outcome_set(w)}'))\n   572\t    for shared in family.get('shared', []):\n   573\t        want = _key(shared)\n   574\t        nodes = [f for f in figs.values() if _key(f['what']) == want and f['basis'] == 'forecast']\n   575\t        touched = [v for v, o in outcomes.items() if any(_key(figs[f]['what']) == want for f in reachable(o))]\n   576\t        if not touched:\n   577\t            continue\n   578\t        per_scenario = {}\n   579\t        for n in nodes:\n   580\t            per_scenario.setdefault(n.get('scenario', 'base'), []).append(n['id'])\n   581\t        if not nodes:\n   582\t            errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: no forecast node, though {\", \".join(touched)} depend on it'))\n   583\t        for sc, ids in sorted(per_scenario.items()):\n   584\t            if len(ids) != 1:\n   585\t                errors.append(('C4', f'{want} {sc}: {len(ids)} forecast nodes ({\", \".join(ids)}); exactly one per scenario is required'))\n   586\t        stop = {n['id'] for n in nodes}\n   587\t        for f in figs.values():                       # [46i.1] scenario membership is derived along the whole path, not declared\n   588\t            sc = f.get('scenario', 'base')\n   589\t            if sc == 'range' or f['kind'] not in ('computed', 'estimate'):\n   590\t                continue\n   591\t            upstream = _upstream_of(f['id'], figs, refs)\n   592\t            borrowed = sorted(r for r in upstream if r in stop and figs[r].get('scenario', 'base') != sc)\n   593\t            if borrowed:\n   594\t                errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: {f[\"id\"]} ({sc}) depends on {\", \".join(borrowed)} of another scenario'))\n   595\t        for view_id in touched:                      # [46g.3] a bypass reaches the quantity through no forecast node of any scenario\n   596\t            bypass = [f for f in reachable(outcomes[view_id], stop=stop) if f not in stop and _key(figs[f]['what']) == want]\n   597\t            if bypass:\n   598\t                errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: {view_id} reaches {\", \".join(sorted(bypass))} without passing a forecast node ({\", \".join(sorted(stop))})'))\n   599\t    for rel in family.get('relations', []):           # [46j.2] the later member rests on the earlier member's forecast nodes, per scenario\n   675\t    units = [i for i in ins if i['what']['measure'] == 'units' and i['unit'] == 'units']\n   676\t    return same and len(price) == 1 and len(units) == 1 and fig['unit'] in ('USD', 'USD bn')\n   677\t\n   678\t\n   679\tdef member_sources(answer, figs):\n   680\t    \"\"\"[46k.3, 46ac.1] The source figures a member's own outcome and reference rest on, each identified by its passage, expression and\n   681\t    the component used.\"\"\"\n   682\t    refs = lambda f: list(f.get('inputs', [])) + [r for r in f.get('rests_on', []) if r in figs] + \\\n   683\t        ([f['adjusts']['figure']] if f.get('adjusts') else []) + ([f['bridge']] if f.get('bridge') else [])\n   684\t    own = set()\n   685\t    for start in (answer.get('outcome'), (answer.get('reference') or {}).get('figure')):\n   686\t        if start in figs:\n   687\t            own |= _upstream_of(start, figs, refs) | {start}\n   688\t    return sorted(f'{figs[f][\"evidence\"]}|{figs[f][\"expression\"]}|{figs[f].get(\"component\", \"value\")}' for f in own if figs[f]['kind'] == 'source')\n   689\t\n   690\t\n   730\t\n   731\t\n   732\tdef publish_decision(family, calc, result):\n   733\t    \"\"\"DESIGN.md §4: 'refused' when a check fails (the harness retries once); 'held' when a member is unresolved and a declared\n   734\t    relation joins it to another member; else 'publish' (unresolved members shown as unresolved).\"\"\"\n   735\t    if result['errors']:\n   736\t        return 'refused'\n   737\t    unresolved = {a['view_id'] for a in calc['answers'] if a.get('shape') == 'unresolved'}\n   738\t    for rel in family.get('relations', []):\n   739\t        ends = {rel.get('part'), rel.get('whole'), rel.get('later'), rel.get('earlier')} - {None}\n   740\t        if ends & unresolved and ends - unresolved:\n   741\t            return 'held'\n   742\t    return 'publish'\n   743\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json,pathlib,re,collections\nroot=pathlib.Path('\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'\\\\'');sys.path.insert(0,str(root))\nimport calc_check as cc\np=json.loads((root/'\\\\''paid-plan.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nfor pattern in [r'\\\\''\\\\b(?:fell|declined|dropped|down)\\\\s+(?:by\\\\s+)?\\\\d+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?%'\\\\'',r'\\\\''not\\\\s+(?:more than|over|less than)\\\\s+\\\\\"'$'\"'\\\\'',r'\\\\''(?:roughly|near|approximately)\\\\s+(?:double|twice)'\\\\'',r'\\\\''US\\\\\"'$3.5'\"\\\\s+billion'\\\\'',r'\\\\''between\\\\s+\\\\\"'$'\"'\\\\'',r'\\\\''\\\\b(?:abov[e]|greater than|at a minimum|upwards of)\\\\s+\\\\\"'$'\"'\\\\'']:\n print(pattern)\n items= {(k,v['\\\\''text'\\\\'']) for i in p for k,v in i['\\\\''passages'\\\\''].items() if re.search(pattern,v['\\\\''text'\\\\''],re.I)}\n for k,v in sorted(items)[:10]: print(k,v)\nfor op,ins,out in [('\\\\''product'\\\\'',[(-3,-2,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\''),(2,4,'\\\\''x'\\\\'')],'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\''),('\\\\''ratio'\\\\'',[(10,10,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\''),(-1,1,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'')],'\\\\''x'\\\\''),('\\\\''sum'\\\\'',[(108,108,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\''),(2,2,'\\\\''%'\\\\'')],'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'')]:\n print(op,cc._compute(op,ins,None,out))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json,pathlib,re,collections\nroot=pathlib.Path('\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'\\\\'');sys.path.insert(0,str(root))\nimport calc_check as cc\np=json.loads((root/'\\\\''paid-plan.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nfor pattern in [r'\\\\''\\\\b(?:fell|declined|dropped|down)\\\\s+(?:by\\\\s+)?\\\\d+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?%'\\\\'',r'\\\\''not\\\\s+(?:more than|over|less than)\\\\s+\\\\\"'$'\"'\\\\'',r'\\\\''(?:roughly|near|approximately)\\\\s+(?:double|twice)'\\\\'',r'\\\\''US\\\\\"'$3.5'\"\\\\s+billion'\\\\'',r'\\\\''between\\\\s+\\\\\"'$'\"'\\\\'',r'\\\\''\\\\b(?:abov[e]|greater than|at a minimum|upwards of)\\\\s+\\\\\"'$'\"'\\\\'']:\n print(pattern)\n items= {(k,v['\\\\''text'\\\\'']) for i in p for k,v in i['\\\\''passages'\\\\''].items() if re.search(pattern,v['\\\\''text'\\\\''],re.I)}\n for k,v in sorted(items)[:10]: print(k,v)\nfor op,ins,out in [('\\\\''product'\\\\'',[(-3,-2,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\''),(2,4,'\\\\''x'\\\\'')],'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\''),('\\\\''ratio'\\\\'',[(10,10,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\''),(-1,1,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'')],'\\\\''x'\\\\''),('\\\\''sum'\\\\'',[(108,108,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\''),(2,2,'\\\\''%'\\\\'')],'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'')]:\n print(op,cc._compute(op,ins,None,out))'\"","aggregated_output":"\\b(?:fell|declined|dropped|down)\\s+(?:by\\s+)?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?%\nnot\\s+(?:more than|over|less than)\\s+\\$\n(?:roughly|near|approximately)\\s+(?:double|twice)\ne2951 CFO Colette Kress explained that customer forecasts actually point to potential growth rates near double the guided 70%, but severe supply chain bottlenecks—ranging from memory availability to data center power and construction—are capping the company's near-term output.\ne5010 As Databricks CEO Ali Ghodsi explained to TechCrunch , two agent systems built around the same model can produce dramatically different bills. Choose the wrong setup, and the same task may cost roughly twice as much to complete.\ne5299 Nvidia ( NASDAQ:NVDA ) CEO Jensen Huang expects the company to sell roughly twice as many chips next year as it does this year, pointing to continued demand for artificial intelligence technology across industries.\nUS\\$3.5\\s+billion\nbetween\\s+\\$\ne3346 For the third quarter, Nvidia expects revenue between $105.84 billion and $110.16 billion, representing year-over-year growth of 85.7% to 93.2% from the $57.01 billion reported in the same quarter last year.\n\\b(?:abov[e]|greater than|at a minimum|upwards of)\\s+\\$\ne2535 With cloud industry backlog now greater than $2 trillion, CapEx by the top 5 hyperscalers is expected to reach nearly $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\nproduct (-6.0, -8.0)\nratio (10.0, -10.0)\nsum (110, 110)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib,re\nroot=pathlib.Path('\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'\\\\''); plan=json.loads((root/'\\\\''paid-plan.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nfor i in plan[-3:]:\n print(i['\\\\''unit'\\\\''])\n for k,v in i['\\\\''passages'\\\\''].items():\n  if re.search(r'\\\\''3.5 billion|25 billion|18 billion|10 billion|1.08 trillion|1.05 trillion'\\\\'',v['\\\\''text'\\\\''],re.I): print(k,v['\\\\''text'\\\\''])\nrun=pathlib.Path('\\\\''poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22'\\\\'')\nfor n,r in enumerate((run/'\\\\''answers.jsonl'\\\\'').open(),1):\n r=json.loads(r)\n if n==20:\n  for g in r['\\\\''data'\\\\'']['\\\\''figures'\\\\'']:\n   if '\\\\''3.5'\\\\'' in str(g.get('\\\\''expression'\\\\'')): print('\\\\''O stored'\\\\'',g)\nfor n,r in enumerate((run/'\\\\''retries.jsonl'\\\\'').open(),1):\n r=json.loads(r)\n if n==10 or n==22 or n==44:\n  print(n,r['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],r.get('\\\\''errors'\\\\''))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib,re\nroot=pathlib.Path('\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'\\\\''); plan=json.loads((root/'\\\\''paid-plan.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nfor i in plan[-3:]:\n print(i['\\\\''unit'\\\\''])\n for k,v in i['\\\\''passages'\\\\''].items():\n  if re.search(r'\\\\''3.5 billion|25 billion|18 billion|10 billion|1.08 trillion|1.05 trillion'\\\\'',v['\\\\''text'\\\\''],re.I): print(k,v['\\\\''text'\\\\''])\nrun=pathlib.Path('\\\\''poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22'\\\\'')\nfor n,r in enumerate((run/'\\\\''answers.jsonl'\\\\'').open(),1):\n r=json.loads(r)\n if n==20:\n  for g in r['\\\\''data'\\\\'']['\\\\''figures'\\\\'']:\n   if '\\\\''3.5'\\\\'' in str(g.get('\\\\''expression'\\\\'')): print('\\\\''O stored'\\\\'',g)\nfor n,r in enumerate((run/'\\\\''retries.jsonl'\\\\'').open(),1):\n r=json.loads(r)\n if n==10 or n==22 or n==44:\n  print(n,r['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],r.get('\\\\''errors'\\\\''))'\"","aggregated_output":"single-O\ne2620 These include equity investments of $99 billion and equity investment commitments of $25 billion as of July 26, 2026.\ne2889 The company said Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of its fiscal year, on top of $47.9 billion it already holds in private companies.\ne3474 NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ: NVDA ) is investing $3.5 billion in Taiwan-based MediaTek through convertible bonds, taking an existing AI partnership a step further.\ne3917 The company also reported a further $25 billion in equity investment commitments as of July 26.\ne4053 The company reported that, as of the end of the quarter, it had about $99 billion invested in shares of other companies, as well as another $25 billion in commitments for future investments.\ne4486 In late February, OpenAI announced $110 billion of new investment at a $730 billion pre-money valuation, including $30 billion each from Nvidia and SoftBank Group and $50 billion from Amazon.\ne4648 Nvidia could invest as much as $10 billion\ne4669 According to a Reuters exclusive , the chipmaker is weighing a US$10 billion commitment to the offering, serving as an early backer that could signal strong institutional confidence to public markets preparing to absorb the astronomical valuations and capital demands of frontier artificial intelligence labs.\nsingle-S\ne1926 What analysts expect the hyperscalers to spend in 2027 alone has more than doubled in the space of a year, from a consensus of $480 billion (€416bn) in August 2025 to $1.08 trillion (€943bn) this month, a rise of about 127%, according to Bank of America.\ne4739 before pushing that figure to $1.08 trillion in 2027.\nsingle-E\nO stored {'id': 'f3', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'announced purchase of convertible bonds', 'scope': 'MediaTek', 'period': 'announced 2026-08-31'}, 'basis': 'guidance', 'scenario': 'announced transaction after the July 26 reporting date', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 3.5, 'low': None, 'high': None, 'bound': None, 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'NVIDIA announced it would buy US$3.5 billion of MediaTek bonds convertible into shares.', 'expression': 'US$3.5 billion', 'component': 'value', 'inputs': None, 'operation': None, 'signs': None, 'relation': None, 'disputed': None, 'bridge': None, 'basis_text': None, 'rests_on': None, 'adjusts': None, 'converts': None}\n10 pair-old-2 [['C7', 'fy27_q3_guidance: a figure needs either a value or a complete range with low at most high']]\n22 single-S [['C7', 'fig_v6_forecast refers to My estimate discounts the top-five all-capex projection for the fifth company and for capital expenditures outside data centers. The evidence does not quantify either adjustment, so this is a judgmental conversion rather than an arithmetic identity., which is not defined']]\n44 single-O [['C1', 'f1: evidence NVIDIA reported $25 billion of equity investment commitments as of 2026-07-26. was not shown'], ['C1', 'f2: evidence NVIDIA said it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of its fiscal year. was not shown'], ['C1', 'f3: evidence NVIDIA announced it would buy US$3.5 billion of MediaTek bonds convertible into shares. was not shown'], ['C2', 'f4: its inputs are points, but it is declared a bound (approx)'], ['C8', 'f4: overlap_unknown must name a disputed operand among its inputs'], ['C7', 'v29: outcome $46.5 billion is not a figure']]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
